    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35958": {
      "title": "Dining Services Hospitality Associate  -Villanova or Radnor, PA",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Dining Services Hospitality Associate  -Villanova or Radnor, PA Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Dining Services Hospitality Associate  -Villanova or Radnor, PA To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedules available include: Full Time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Sunday - Thursday 4:30 pm – 1:30 am 2.) Sunday - Thursday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 3.) Tuesday – Saturday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 4.) Friday – Monday 6:00 am – 5:00 pm 5.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 6.) Sunday - Thursday 6am - 3pm 7.) Sunday - Thursday 12pm - 9pm Full time, 9 months (9-month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 3pm – 12 am Part time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Monday and Friday 4pm – 9pm. Saturday and Sunday 12pm – 9pm. 2.) Tuesday – Saturday 9am -2:30pm 3.) Sunday and Monday 9am – 2:30pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 12pm – 5:30pm 4.) Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday, and Sunday 6am - 3pm Part time, 9 months (9 month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 5pm – 10:30pm 2.) Monday – Friday 7:30 am – 1pm. Please note in your application which shift(s) you are available to work. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260342S Position Title: Dining Services Hospitality Associate  -Villanova or Radnor, PA Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: Varies Avg Hours Week Department: 411-Dining Services Administration Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Villanova University’s new Cabrini Campus will open in August 2026 ! To learn more about the 112-acre campus, including information on the shuttle bus service, please visit the Villanova University, Cabrini Campus page by clicking here. Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . As a member of the Dining Services Department, the individual will work in any of the following positions: front of the house- food production/serving/cashier/barista and back of the house food production. As a Dining Services Hospitality Associate, you will serve customers in an efficient and courteous manner. The Dining Services Hospitality Associate will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. The individual will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, and Excellence . All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Why join our team? Our dining services team members receive: Increased hourly rate starting at $17.50/hour Generous vacation plan and holiday schedule Free meals during each shift Health and wellness resources plus discount programs Opportunities for advancement Various schedules available, including late-night positions with night differential Free uniforms, including footwear *Full-time employees also receive: 403b retirement plan with employer base and matching contributions, tuition remission for associates and dependents, medical, vision, and dental insurance with multiple health plan options Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Set-up, maintain, and break down all service lines. Ability to prepare and/or cook food for cold production and for pizza/grill lines. Stock, rotate and replenish merchandise as needed. Back of the house production includes salad and fruit bars, deli prep, desserts, and commissary items May work on any of the following stations serving our customers: sandwich/salad/pizza/grill/Holy Grounds areas/register stations Serves customers in an efficient and courteous manner in accordance with our mission. Responsible for serving the proper proportions and following all safety and sanitation practices. Is familiar with all menu items and recipes following our standards. Cleans and sanitizes food equipment and dining room tables and chairs NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Works special events/weekends as required Assists in the dish room area if needed including sweeping, mopping, disposing of trash/recycling Perform additional job duties as directed by supervisor or manager Minimum Qualifications: Work Skills: Basic reading and writing skills; basic communication skills Excellent customer service skills Practices excellent personal hygiene habits and follows and adheres to uniform standards Ability to: follow directions and complete assigned tasks, work with minimal supervision, and to interact with people on a constant basis Preferred Qualifications: Preferred – High school diploma or equivalent Preferred – Basic knowledge of food service safety and sanitation Preferred – Serv Safe Training and Allergy Awareness Training Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Knives, slicers, and all kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: Chemicals used for cleaning Weather exposure for special events Physical requirements: Ability to stand for extended periods Ability to lift, push/pull up to 10 pounds independently and up to 40 pounds with assistance Ability to withstand extreme temperatures Special Message to Applicants: Schedules available include: Full Time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 4:30 pm – 1:30 am 2.) Sunday – Thursday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 3.) Tuesday – Saturday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 4.) Friday – Monday 6:00 am – 5:00 pm 5.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 6.) Sunday – Thursday 6am – 3pm 7.) Sunday – Thursday 12pm – 9pm Full time, 9 months (9-month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 3pm – 12 am Part time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Monday and Friday 4pm – 9pm. Saturday and Sunday 12pm – 9pm. 2.) Tuesday – Saturday 9am -2:30pm 3.) Sunday and Monday 9am – 2:30pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 12pm – 5:30pm 4.) Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday, and Sunday 6am – 3pm Part time, 9 months (9 month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 5pm – 10:30pm 2.) Monday – Friday 7:30 am – 1pm. Please note in your application which shift(s) you are available to work. Posting Date: 07/13/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $17.50 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 1 Maximum Number of References Needed 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Which shift(s) are you available to work? Please select all that apply. Sunday - Thursday 4:30 pm - 1:30am Sunday - Thursday 4pm - 1:00am Tuesday-Saturday 4pm-1am Friday - Monday 6am - 5pm Friday-Monday 2pm-1am (2 openings) Monday/Tuesday/Wednesday/Saturday 9am - 6pm. Friday 7am - 4pm Sunday - Thursday 3pm - 12am Monday and Friday 4pm - 9pm. Saturday and Sunday 12pm - 9pm Tuesday - Saturday 9am - 2:30pm Sunday and Monday 9am - 2:30pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 12pm - 5:30pm Sunday - Thursday 5pm - 10:30pm Monday - Friday 7:30am - 1pm * Please select the location you are interested in working at (select all that apply) Cabrini Campus (Radnor PA) Villanova Campus (Villanova PA) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
