    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35789": {
      "title": "Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Night (3rd) Shift: 10pm - 6:30am; Sunday-Thursday Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260369S Position Title: Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 809-Custodial Services Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Under the moderate direction of a supervisor, performs general cleaning duties within dormitory, office, and other public facilities areas. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: TYPICAL JOB DUTIES Pick up and dispose of trash, to include the proper handling of recyclable materials. Dusts, sweeps, and/or dry mops. Wet mops and/or spot mops. Operates walk-behind or ride-on floor machine, wet vac, & carpet extractor. • Cleans glass: • All inside areas that can be safely reached. All entrance glass, including doors, inside and out. Sanitizes washrooms, showers, and toilet facilities (dormitories only). Fills all dispensers in restrooms. Vacuums and cleans carpets and walk-off mats. • Washes walls, woodwork, light fixtures, inside of windows, and other glass. Removes snow and ice and cleans and/or picks up debris, such as leaves and paper, around entrances and fire exits (including fire escapes [dormitories only]) from the steps, and from the steps and walkways (generally distanced of ten feet or less) leading to buildings. Reports to immediate supervisor or to work control damage and/or malfunction of equipment observed within assigned areas. Performs other duties assigned within the normal scope of the department’s responsibilities and the individual’s capabilities. Minimum Qualifications: H.S. Diploma or equivalent Ability to follow both written and oral directions. Ability to interact with customers(students, faculty, administration), co-workers and supervisors in a positive and helpful manner. Must be able to climb ladders, to bend and reach, and to lift(up to 60 lbs.) Preferred Qualifications: H.S. Diploma or equivalent. 1 to 3 years of experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Must be able to climb ladders, bend and reach, and lift up to 60 lbs. Special Message to Applicants: Night (3rd) Shift: 10pm – 6:30am; Sunday-Thursday Posting Date: 07/21/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $19.97+$1.75 shift differential = $21.72 an hour Salary Grade: UNION Job Classification: union References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36120": {
      "title": "Information Technology Technician I",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Information Technology Technician I - Application Developer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Information Technology Technician I - Application Developer To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260352V Position Title: Information Technology Technician I - Application Developer Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Kennedy Hall Detailed Work Schedule During business hours, Monday – Friday 9AM-5PM. Number of positions: 3 Department: 723-UTS-Web Services and Technologies Contact Name: Mujtaba Talebi Contact Phone/Extension: N/A Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Are you looking for real-world technical experience in a collaborative and supportive environment? Join the Web Services and Technologies ( WST ) team within University Technology Services ( UTS )! As an IT Technician I – Application Developer you may support WST with application development support, quality assurance, content updates, and enterprise technology initiatives development tasks that improve the University’s digital services for the Villanova community in alignment with the TechNova strategic plan and depending on current needs . This position is designed for students who want to gain practical hands-on experience with web platforms, technologies and enterprise applications, digital forms, mobile technologies, low-code/no-code tools, and emerging AI-supported work while learning from experienced UTS professionals to deliver impactful solutions for the Villanova community. Students in this role will develop practical experience with professional communication, service management, quality assurance, documentation, application support, and collaborative problem solving in a higher education technology environment. Example responsibilities (students may perform work on different tasks, including but not limited to, the following based on departmental needs ): Assist with maintenance and enhancement of the University website and web portal, including content updates and functionality improvements. Perform quality checks for broken links, spelling errors, and accessibility compliance. Create and update digital content and assets for end users. Maintain and organize the Document Asset Management ( DAM ) repository, ensuring accuracy and consistency. Support content lifecycle management, including removal, archiving, and migration of assets. Assist with development and testing of University mobile applications. Work on integrations and supporting web applications. Conduct routine audits of mobile application content for permissions, relevancy, and accuracy; resolve broken links and outdated content. Assist with development and maintenance of low-code/no-code applications. Work on AI- related initiatives. Contribute to documentation efforts, including technical guides and process workflows. Monitor and manage Service Request/Incident queue, ensuring timely updates and resolution. Requirements: General technical curiosity, comfort learning new systems, knowledge and familiarity with Microsoft Office 365 are required. Interest or experience in one or more of the following areas is helpful: content management systems, customer relationship management platforms, mobile applications, web analytics, enterprise applications, document imaging, digital forms, workflows, integrations, artificial intelligence, or low-code/no-code application development. Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Open to both undergraduateUndergraduate and graduateGraduate students; candidates available year-round are preferred. Training will be provided by UTS . Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: May occasionally need to lift/move computer equipment Wage Rate: 11.25 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work during the summer? Yes No Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33411": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Philosophy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Philosophy To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Philosophy Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. Online applications must include: ** A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. ** A letter of interest. The letter should include the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. ** Past Syllabi. If the applicant wishes, any additional supporting documents may be submitted online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020703F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Philosophy Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 141-Philosophy Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Philosophy for undergraduate courses only. The applicant must be committed to excellence in the teaching of philosophy. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester and openings to teach these courses develop on a periodic basis, depending on department teaching needs. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: A master’s degree is required. Preferred Qualifications: * An earned doctorate in philosophy is strongly preferred. * Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Philosophy Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. Online applications must include: * A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. * A letter of interest. The letter should include the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. ** Past Syllabi. If the applicant wishes, any additional supporting documents may be submitted online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document Optional Documents Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
