    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34117": {
      "title": "Center for Speaking and Presentation: Undergraduate Tutor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Center for Speaking and Presentation: Undergraduate Tutor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Center for Speaking and Presentation: Undergraduate Tutor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255436V Position Title: Center for Speaking and Presentation: Undergraduate Tutor Posting Type Student Hours/week: 4-10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Falvey Memorial Library Detailed Work Schedule Tutors perform 4-10 weekly hours which will include tasks like tutoring in Speaking and Presentation skills as well as staffing tabling events, running workshops, and performing class visits. Number of positions: 6 Department: 126-Tutoring Center Contact Name: Juliana Studer Contact Phone/Extension: 6105195862 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: * Run tutoring sessions for public speakers. Session types (approx. 60-minutes in length, focused on a single area or combination, depending on individual needs) * Technologies: competency with WCOnline tutor scheduling platform Topics covered during a session may include: audience analysis, eye contact, vocal projection, managing speaking anxiety, critiquing visual aids, etc. Attending monthly tutor training events presenting workshops and class visits staffing resource fair tables (three events annually: august, february, april) Requirements: Must be a COM major Must have a cumulative GPA of 3.3 or above Provide contact information of at least one Villanova faculty member who can provide an endorsement Must have completed Public Speaking class by start date for the semester Additional Information: Past peer mentoring or peer tutoring experience prefered but not required. Physical Demands Summary: Being physically on campus to run sessions out of Falvey Library. Wage Rate: $11.25/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
