    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35293": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor or Instructor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor or Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor or Instructor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. We invite you to apply by June 26, 2026, for full consideration. All applications are to include: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Copies of academic transcripts (undergraduate and graduate). Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Three letters of recommendation. An email will be sent to each of your references with a secure web link asking that they submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. For finalists, an official graduate transcript and a statement of contribution to Villanova’s mission will be required. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260040F Position Title: Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor or Instructor Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 185-Mathematics & Statistics Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Villanova University welcomes applications for a nine-month visiting teaching position spanning Fall 2026 and Spring 2027, at the rank of either Assistant Teaching Professor (for those with a PhD) or Instructor. The teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The primary duties are to foundational courses in mathematics and/or statistics. Teaching upper-level courses is also possible. Our department currently has 45 full-time faculty members and is known for its collegiality. Our faculty are engaged and supportive, and strive to foster academic excellence. The Department provides a caring community in which students of all backgrounds can learn and succeed. Further information can be found at https://math.villanova.edu . Villanova is located 12 miles west of Philadelphia, which is the nation’s sixth largest city and home to many historical and cultural attractions. There is easy access to the Philadelphia International Airport and to nearby cities such as New York and Washington, DC both by highway and by rail. More information about Villanova and its location is available on the Villanova website at https://www1.villanova.edu/university.html . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach 12 credit hours (three or four courses) per semester in person. Participate in the life of the department. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field; Strong teaching ability. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field; Exceptional teaching ability. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. We invite you to apply by June 26, 2026, for full consideration. All applications are to include: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Copies of academic transcripts (undergraduate and graduate). Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Three letters of recommendation. An email will be sent to each of your references with a secure web link asking that they submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. For finalists, an official graduate transcript and a statement of contribution to Villanova’s mission will be required. Posting Date: 06/08/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 4 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Summary of Teaching Evaluations Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35902": {
      "title": "Storeroom Keeper",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Storeroom Keeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Storeroom Keeper To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260144V Position Title: Storeroom Keeper Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 20 hrs/week with courses, up to 40 hrs/week without Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Mendel Science Center Detailed Work Schedule Summer 26 Storeroom Hours: Monday – Thursday 9:00am – 5:00pm Fall 26 Storeroom Hours: Monday – Wednesday 7:30am – 9:30pm Thursday – Friday 7:30am – 6:00pm subject to change Spring 27 Storeroom Hours: Monday – Wednesday 7:30am – 9:30pm Thursday – Friday 7:30am – 6:00pm subject to change Number of positions: up to 25 Department: 184-Chemistry Contact Name: Joseph Kasopsky Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5278 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Clean and set up labs, issue and receive equipment, file, deliver items to other departments, and other office duties as required. Students enter data in order to track and maintain storeroom chemicals while overseeing storeroom security. Supervise and assist with chemical check-out process. Prepare small and safe reagents and supply them for labs (1103, 1108, i.e. Zinc & Cooper strips). Prepare disposable pipettes for experiments. The Storeroom Keeper is the first visible contact that is trained on safety procedures and has the proper contact info and location for the on-duty safety officer. Requirements: Additional Information: Please indicate which semester you are applying to work: Summer, Fall, or Spring. Please include only your workable schedule not class schedule in the application, as well as your minimum and maximum hours preferred per week. In addition to applying online, please indicate a convenient time for Joseph Kasopksy to call you for a brief phone interview. Training will be provided. Only apply after you know your workable schedule in order to look at your open time slots. Physical Demands Summary: Some lifting required. Wage Rate: $11.25 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 04/25/2027 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
