    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34843": {
      "title": "Nursing Clinical Skills Specialist",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Nursing Clinical Skills Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Nursing Clinical Skills Specialist To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. NA Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260022T Position Title: Nursing Clinical Skills Specialist Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: casual/seasonal Approximate Number of Hours per Week Less than 20 hrs per week Department: 232-Nursing Position Summary: The M. Louise Fitzpatrick College of Nursing seeks applicants for the role of Nursing Clinical Skills Specialist. The Nursing Clinical Skills Specialist performs diverse duties in the Dee Adams Center for Innovation and Simulation Excellence and serves as a resource to support student, faculty and staff needs. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Simulation Support Services Serves as a resource to support students, faculty, and staff with simulation activities in the Dee Adams Center for Innovation and Simulation Excellence using the Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best Practice ™: Assists with simulation event set-up and break down; facilitation of simulation events including prebriefing and debriefing; assists with manikin scenario programming and fidelity; operates simulation-related equipment (medication dispensing machines, electronic health record, etc.); troubleshoots equipment for problem resolution; participates in inventorying and replenishing supplies; seeks resources for simulation experiences. Simulation Scenario Maintenance Utilizing nursing and simulation knowledge, assists Executive Director and Associate Director in updating and maintaining simulation scenarios and related materials to keep with current nursing practice standards and Healthcare Standards of Best Practice ™. Faculty and Student Simulation Support Supports Executive Director and Associate Director with administrative responsibilities including but not limited to: evaluation/revision of simulation experiences; orientation of faculty to simulation experiences; orientation of graduate students to responsibilities in the Dee Adams Center for Innovation and Simulation Excellence; assistance with student skill development. Minimum Qualifications: RN with a minimum of Bachelor’s of Science in Nursing required. Minimum two (2) years clinical experience required. Excellent troubleshooting skills, excellent oral and written communication skills and strong organizational and interpersonal skills required. Ability to function independently with minimal supervision. Interest (in learning about) in developing scenarios for simulation models. Must convey a highly professional demeanor and be a team player, and demonstrate excellent customer service skills. Must have the ability to handle a fast-paced environment and manage multiple projects/tasks with varied deadlines and frequent interruptions. Must be able to work independently and be a strong problem solver. Knowledge of and interest in nursing simulation technical applications. Computer literacy in Microsoft Office programs required. Knowledge of computer operations – including Sim man and/or other high fidelity manikins. Microsoft Office applications Microsoft Office programs, audio-visual recording systems, LCD Projectors. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s of Science in Nursing preferred Minimum three (3) years teaching experience and/or working with simulation models preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: NA EEO Statement Posting Date: 04/08/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $29.97-33.50/hr. Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35804": {
      "title": "Senior Buyer",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Senior Buyer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Senior Buyer To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260377S Position Title: Senior Buyer Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 435-Procurement Office Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Senior Buyer is responsible for the procurement of a wide range of commodities, materials, supplies, equipment, and services in support of the University’s operational and academic needs. This position analyzes university spending data to determine sourcing opportunities, develop procurement strategies, and establish long-term supplier partnerships that maximize value, improve service, and achieve cost efficiencies. The Senior Buyer focuses on providing the best value contracts for the University through sourcing new suppliers and negotiating with current suppliers. The Senior Buyer prepares detailed bid specifications, requests for quotations and proposals for commodities and services, and reviews purchase order requests ensuring that the purchases are following University policies and providing the best overall value to the University. The Senior Buyer applies advanced analytical, critical thinking and written communication skills in the development and evaluation of the more complex requests for proposals for commodities and services. In addition, the Senior Buyer reviews purchase requisitions to ensure compliance with University policies and procurement standards, issues purchase orders, develops service standards for new products and services, maintains strong supplier relationships and maintains comprehensive descriptions of available products and current prices. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsible for procuring a variety of services and products including capital equipment. Senior Buyer is responsible for creating RFP documentation, issuance and analysis of bid specifications, evaluation of bid packages for accuracy and compliance, and providing support to end users during the bid process and contract negotiation. Senior Buyers will ensure all RFPs, Contracts, and Purchase Orders are in compliance with all City, State, and Federal laws, codes, and regulations and University policies and procedures, and provide customer service for campus purchasers as requested. Survey and research product information and market trends with responsibility for commodity purchases involving large and/or difficult expenditures of a technical and/or complex nature. Investigate sources of supply; interview and correspond with suppliers. Research and assist in the development of pricing for university department planning purposes. Develop bid documents, review, and analyze technical specifications and product standards for complex equipment purchases and service contracts; direct the selection of interested and qualified suppliers. Conduct pre-bid conferences to address concerns and provide direction to interested bidders; analyze bid packages to ensure compliance to specifications, completeness of supporting documentation, accuracy, and compliance with applicable rules and regulations. Negotiate contracts with suppliers with the support of General Counsel, Risk Management and Information Security. Form cross-functional teams in order to qualify suppliers and develop long term acquisition plans for various materials and services. Analyze University spending data to determine commodities and /or departments to work with to establish long-term supplier partnership agreements. Continually negotiate with these suppliers for long-term agreements and quality improvement solutions. Review and evaluate purchase requisitions for accuracy from campus departments. Determine preferred suppliers and best method needed for fulfillment. Ensure all contracts are reviewed and are in compliance with University policies. Maintain a detailed knowledge of the products and services being procured and supplier/procurement alternatives, via a proactive and productive relationship with suppliers and manufacturers. Coordinate campus-wide service and maintenance contracts for university owned equipment and services. Meet with established and prospective suppliers to update current goods and services available, and to review pricing structure in place. Maintain strong working relationships with current suppliers to assure quality service. Advise all levels of personnel (Deans, Directors, Faculty and Staff) regarding purchase and supply requirements, policies and procedures, specifications, quality of products and delivery needs. Serve on a variety of committees to meet procurement strategic goals. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Four-year college degree preferred or equivalent job experience. Specific Job Knowledge: Thorough knowledge of purchasing and procurement practices, including competitive sourcing and vendor selection. Experience in University or other service-oriented environment. Ability to interpret and apply University purchasing policies and procedures. Knowledge of sources and types of products and services commonly used in a university setting. Experience with methods of conducting product and supplier research. Ability to assist varying levels throughout the University and provide excellent customer service in a timely and responsive manner, providing accurate and thorough information and guidance. Strong attention to detail with the ability to analyze pricing, specifications, and vendor documentation. Proficiency with procurement and financial systems (e.g., Concur or similar systems) and standard office software. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Effective communication and interpersonal skills to work collaboratively with university departments and external vendors. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and deliver superior customer service to varying levels throughout the University in a timely and responsive manner, providing accurate and thorough information and guidance. Experienced in creating and editing reports in Excel. Skilled in negotiating issues and resolving problems. Work Experience: At least five years of experience is required in procurement, preferably in the education or not-for-profit sector, with specific experience in the preparation of highly technical and/or complex solicitation documents for the procurement of commodities and services and in using automated procurement systems and processes. Work Skills: Strong analytical skills, collecting and analyzing complex data, evaluating information and systems, and drawing logical conclusions. Ability for establishing priorities for areas of operational improvement and development and executing a plan of action. Ability to structure and prioritize work to achieve specific deliverables in an environment characterized by tight deadlines and competing and frequently changing priorities. Strong interpersonal skills and communication skills. Ability to analyze and solve problems. Ability to handle high volume of activity with high degree of accuracy, and strong data entry skills. Ability to work with limited supervision; self-motivated. Ability to interpret, communicate, and enforce financial policies with professionalism. Advanced Excel and financial systems proficiency. Customer-service mindset with ability to work effectively across all levels of the University. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: Four-year college degree preferred or equivalent job experience. Work Experience: At least five years of experience is required in procurement, preferably in the education or not-for-profit sector. Experience leading high-value sourcing events. Work Skills: Knowledge of higher education procurement practices. Experience with consortium purchasing (E&I, OMNIA Partners, Sourcewell, COSTARS , PA State Contract, etc.). Experience supporting research, facilities, IT, and academic departments. Specific Job Knowledge: Demonstrated success negotiating complex contracts resulting in measurable cost savings and improved supplier performance. Experience developing and managing competitive RFP , RFQ , and RFI processes. Strong understanding of higher education procurement practices, cooperative purchasing agreements, and applicable procurement regulations. Proven ability to build collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, suppliers, and executive leadership. Equipment Knowledge Experience with eProcurement systems ( ESM , Concur, Banner, PaymentWorks). Experience with Microsoft Office products is necessary. Ability to build and maintain complex Microsoft Excel spreadsheets. Standard office equipment, including PC and common software packages. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 07/22/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 16 and the range is $71,700-95,000. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 16 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
