    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34063": {
      "title": "CRF Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | CRF Student Ambassador Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us CRF Student Ambassador To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260056V Position Title: CRF Student Ambassador Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Garey Hall Detailed Work Schedule CRF is open 9:00 AM- 5:00 PM Monday through Friday. Students work a minimum of 10 hours per week, typically in 2-4 hour shifts. Number of positions: 1 Department: 165- Office of U/G Research & Fellowships Contact Name: Kate Vicente Contact Phone/Extension: (610) 519-6138 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Summary : The Center for Research and Fellowships ( CRF ) administers three key areas of programming at Villanova University: student research, nationally competitive scholarships and fellowships, and the Presidential Scholars Program ( PSP ). CRF seeks an undergraduate student worker to support general office functions starting in Fall 2026. Student workers will have numerous opportunities to develop professional skills through writing, editing, outreach, and events. This position reports to CRF’s Senior Administrative Assistant. Responsibilities : Front Desk & Operations: Greeting all guests to the CRF -Office of Education Abroad ( OEA ) office suite; checking in appointments; answering in-person and phone inquiries; editorial projects; data projects; supporting CRF staff on programmatic needs. Events: Provide support with events, including the autumn Student Research Symposium, February Presidential Scholars Interview Program. Creating and editing promotional materials. Outreach: Assist in outreach and recruitment of candidates for external scholarships and fellowships, such as the Fulbright U.S. Student Program and other awards. Promote CRF through on-campus tabling and orientation events (occasionally on weekends/evenings). Other duties and projects as assigned. Requirements: Requirements : Students from any major or program on campus are welcome to apply for this position. We are looking for someone with: Strong interpersonal/customer service skills. This role involves frequent interaction with students, staff, and external stakeholders like Villanova applicants, parents, and high school guidance counselors including in person and on the phone An interest in writing, proofreading, and editorial work Willingness to take initiative Reliability, time management, and organizational skills This position requires the ability to discreetly manage sensitive information in accordance with University and FERPA confidentiality guidelines Additional Information: CRF is open 9:00 AM- 5:00 PM Monday through Friday. Students work a minimum of 10 hours per week, typically in 2-4 hour shifts. Physical Demands Summary: The job is physically comfortable and mostly requires a typical desk sitting position. Wage Rate: $13.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 07/09/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35296": {
      "title": "Law Library Access Services Evening/Weekend Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Law Library Access Services Evening/Weekend Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Law Library Access Services Evening/Weekend Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260217V Position Title: Law Library Access Services Evening/Weekend Manager Posting Type Student Hours/week: 4 to 8 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Widger Law School Building Detailed Work Schedule One weekly four hour shift, evenings Monday through Friday and weekends. Number of positions: 7 Department: 243-Law School Library Contact Name: Emma Kearney Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5454 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Learn more about your library! Provide services at the law library circulation/reserve desk. Check IDs, retrieve Reserve materials, check out books, provide basic directional information and make referrals to librarians. Also, perform other tasks such as research and assistance with library projects. Requirements: Must be a rising 2L or 3L law student with commitment to customer service. Priority will be given to 2L students who are interested in working through the next two years and those who have open availability. Additional Information: Applications will be rolling and will continue until all positions are filled. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 15.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a Villanova Law student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
