    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36127": {
      "title": "Athletics Fund Development Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Athletics Fund Development Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Athletics Fund Development Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260354V Position Title: Athletics Fund Development Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: Flexible, including evenings and weekends during football and basketball seasons (approximately 10-20 hours/week during active seasons) Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Riley Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 779-Athl - V Club Contact Name: Megan Kilpatrick Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-6527 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Villanova Athletics Fund ( VAF ) seeks an enthusiastic, customer service-oriented undergraduate student to serve as a Game Day Host & Athletics Development Assistant. This position is primarily responsible for providing exceptional hospitality and guest service to donors, alumni, and special guests during Villanova Football and Men’s and Women’s Basketball home games. The student worker will also support Athletics Advancement operations through donor stewardship activities, event support, research projects, and administrative assistance. This position offers valuable hands-on experience in collegiate athletics, donor relations, fundraising, customer service, event operations, and higher education advancement. Villanova is a Catholic University sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion are integral components of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and contribute to the University’s mission and values. % of Time 70% – Game Day Hospitality & Guest Services Serve as a welcoming representative of the Villanova Athletics Fund at home football and basketball games. Greet and assist donors, alumni, and invited guests at hospitality and premium seating locations. Support game day check-in and credential distribution processes. Assist with hospitality area setup, maintenance, and breakdown. Provide guests with directions, event information, and general game day assistance. Coordinate with Athletics and event staff to ensure an exceptional donor and fan experience. Identify and address guest needs in a professional, courteous, and timely manner. Maintain a positive and enthusiastic presence while representing Villanova University and Athletics Advancement. 25% – Athletics Development Operations & Special Projects Assist with planning and execution of the annual Villanova Athletics Fund Auction and other donor engagement events. Support donor acknowledgment and stewardship efforts, including preparation of thank-you letters and donor correspondence. Conduct research and benchmarking projects related to athletics fundraising, donor recognition, stewardship programs, and peer institution best practices. Assist with data entry, mailings, filing, and general office support. Support special projects and initiatives within Athletics Advancement. 5% – Other Duties Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Requirements: 1. Formal Education: (e.g., degree) Must be a currently enrolled Villanova University undergraduate student. 2. Specific Job Knowledge: (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Excellent organizational and time-management abilities. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Strong attention to detail and follow-through. Interest in athletics, fundraising, event management, sports business, communications, or nonprofit development preferred. 3. Work Skills: Professional demeanor and ability to interact confidently with donors, alumni, university leadership, and guests. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to multitask and remain organized in a fast-paced environment. Strong problem-solving skills and customer-service orientation. 4. Equipment Knowledge: Familiarity with Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word, and Outlook. Experience with donor databases, CRM platforms, or event management systems is a plus. 5. Working Conditions/Environment: a. Tools, machinery and equipment used: General office equipment and event support materials. b. Environmental conditions: Office setting and athletic event venues. c. Physical requirements: Ability to stand and move throughout game day events for extended periods. Ability to lift and transport event materials weighing up to 25 pounds. Position includes evenings and weekends during athletic seasons. Additional Information: Learning Opportunities Through this position, students will gain hands-on experience in: Collegiate athletics fundraising and advancement Donor stewardship and engagement Event planning and operations Customer service and hospitality management Research and benchmarking methodologies Professional communication and office operations Preferred Characteristics The ideal candidate is: Friendly, reliable, and professional Comfortable engaging with a diverse range of guests Passionate about Villanova Athletics Able to thrive in a fast-paced game day environment Interested in athletics administration, fundraising, event management, or higher education advancement Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $ 11.25 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35701": {
      "title": "Catering Delivery Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedule will vary weekly depending on event needs. Must be flexible. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260251S Position Title: Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 838-Cabrini Catering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Catering Delivery Assistant is responsible for the daily operation of catering delivery contracts and ensures that our quality standards are maintained. This includes the driving and operating of the department’s vans. This position is also responsible for the food delivery services in the building and for remote set ups . This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, and Excellence. All our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Deliver catering orders to various campus locations, including academic buildings, residence halls, administrative offices, and event venues. Load, transport, unload, and organize food, beverages, supplies, and catering equipment. Set up buffet lines, beverage stations, meeting refreshments, and event displays according to catering specifications. Verify the accuracy and completeness of orders before delivery and upon setup. Maintain food quality, temperature control, and safe handling practices during transportation and service. Provide courteous and professional customer service to faculty, staff, students, alumni, and guests. Assist with event breakdown, equipment retrieval, and cleanup following catered events. Operate carts, vans, or other approved campus delivery vehicles safely and responsibly. Maintain cleanliness and organization of catering storage areas, vehicles, and equipment. Communicate delivery schedules, special requests, and service issues to supervisors and catering staff. Follow university policies, health and safety regulations, and food service standards. Support other Dining Services operations as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High School Diploma/equivalent or 2+ years of food service experience required. Specific Job Knowledge: Serv Safe certification preferred. Basic knowledge of food service overall. Valid PA Driver License required with a good driving record and no traffic violations. Must be able to meet and maintain VU driving privileges as outlined by Villanova’s Risk Management’s Motor Vehicle Record Policy for Driver’s of University Vehicles. Qualifications: Strong customer service and communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Reliable attendance and punctuality. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings, weekends, and special events Work Skills: Attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and meet deadlines. Professional demeanor when interacting with the campus community and visitors Equipment Knowledge: General kitchen and food service equipment knowledge. How to operate the department vans. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: Kitchen Equipment Vans Environmental Conditions: Chemicals associated with the food service industry. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift up to 30 pounds independently Ability to sit stand for extended periods Ability to push/pull up to 30 pounds independently Ability to use various chemicals Special Message to Applicants: Schedule will vary weekly depending on event needs. Must be flexible. Posting Date: 07/15/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.25 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36071": {
      "title": "Associate General Counsel (Contracts and Data Privacy/Security Compliance)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Associate General Counsel (Contracts and Data Privacy/Security Compliance) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Associate General Counsel (Contracts and Data Privacy/Security Compliance) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation, if a finalist. This is an in-office position. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260396S Position Title: Associate General Counsel (Contracts and Data Privacy/Security Compliance) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 705-VP and General Counsel Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Associate General Counsel is an officer of administration who assists in handling all University legal affairs under the direction of the Vice President and General Counsel. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Under the direction of the Vice President and General Counsel, provides general legal services and day-to-day advice to principal officers of the administration. Drafts, reviews and negotiates complex commercial contracts involving business operations and technology (including software/platform as a service, IT services, software licenses and data processing agreements) and handles all data security/privacy components of contracts. Works directly with the Office of Risk Management, the Office of Information Security, and other relevant partners in the internal contract review process. Counsel internal clients on compliance with applicable federal, state, and international information security and privacy laws and regulations. Advises the Office of Risk Management on a wide range of risk management and liability issues and prepares appropriate contracts, participant releases and waivers. Advises the Office of Grants and Contracts, as needed, on preparation of submissions and filings to governmental agencies in connection with research grants. Advises with respect to research compliance, research integrity, export controls, and research financial conflict of interest, including, but not limited to policy development and updates and serving ex officio on research committees. Oversees and participates in research regulatory proceedings involving the University, managing matters and advising outside counsel. Oversees responses to research inquiries, audits or investigations directed to the University, including gathering records and ensuring compliance with legal requirements regarding confidentiality and proprietary information. Advises with respect to internal dispute resolution and administrative proceedings such as research noncompliance, research misconduct, suspension or termination matters. Assists in intellectual property issues as needed, including patent prosecution efforts and copyright and trademark registration and enforcement issues. Assists in formulating and implementing institutional strategies for avoiding future legal problems. Provides training to personnel as appropriate. Serves on University committees as assigned by the Vice President and General Counsel. Performs additional duties and assists with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Graduation from an accredited law school with a LL.B./J.D. degree. Must be admitted and in good standing in Pennsylvania or other state bar; admission to the Pennsylvania bar required within 1 year of appointment. Work Experience: 4-8 years’ legal practice. Work Skills: Strong time management skills and the ability to prioritize multiple projects. Specific Job Knowledge: Significant demonstrated experience drafting, reviewing and negotiating complex commercial and technology contracts and data privacy and security components. Expertise in U.S., state and international data security and privacy laws and regulatory compliance. Strong time management skills and the ability to prioritize multiple projects. Demonstrated capacity for legal research, analysis and reasoning, superior oral and written communication skills, and an ability to identify and resolve complicated and sensitive problems creatively and with professional discretion. Demonstrated ability to interact and function effectively in an academic community and collaborative team environment. Equipment: General knowledge of word processing equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Work Experience: Work experience in a private research facility or pharmaceutical company. Work experience in advising on or drafting agreements for and overseeing matters involving grants, sponsored research agreements, grant proposals and University-funded research. Work experience in advising on matters of research compliance, research integrity, export controls, and research financial conflict of interest including, but not limited to, developing and updating policy and providing support for research committees. Work experience in overseeing and participating in research regulatory proceedings, managing matters and advising outside counsel. Work experience in overseeing responses to research inquiries, audits or investigations, including gathering records and ensuring compliance with legal requirements regarding confidentiality and proprietary information. Experience in advising with respect to internal research-related dispute resolution and administrative proceedings such as those related to research noncompliance, misconduct, suspension or termination matters. Experience in technology transfer and commercialization. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Sitting for extended periods of time and occasional lifting of legal file boxes. Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation, if a finalist. This is an in-office position. Posting Date: 08/19/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 21 and the range is $191,000-$212,300. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 21 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33397": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Mathematics and Statistics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Mathematics and Statistics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Screening of submitted application begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu. All applications are to include: * Application letter. * Current and complete curriculum vitae. * Copies of transcripts (undergraduate and graduate). * A statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2012062F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Mathematics and Statistics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 185-Mathematics & Statistics Position Summary: The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Villanova University seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach courses in Mathematics or Statistics at the introductory, upper division, or graduate levels. Minimum Qualifications: Masters degree Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Screening of submitted application begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu. All applications are to include: * Application letter. * Current and complete curriculum vitae. * Copies of transcripts (undergraduate and graduate). * A statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: 08/20/2012 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed Maximum Number of References Needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Statement of Teaching Philosophy © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
