    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35016": {
      "title": "Storeroom Keeper",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Storeroom Keeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Storeroom Keeper To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260080V Position Title: Storeroom Keeper Posting Type Student Hours/week: 4-6 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Mendel Science Center Detailed Work Schedule Flexible weekday schedule, between 9am-5pm, no weekends. Number of positions: 2-3 Department: 183-Biology Contact Name: Daniel Dye Contact Phone/Extension: x4858 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Basic lab work; clean glassware; process samples; assist with various types of analysis. Requirements: Attention to detail; able to follow directions; science major preferred, but not required. Previous lab experience a plus. Additional Information: Hands-on training provided. Flexible schedule available. Further training opportunities available, including safety certificates in DOT , OSHA , and EPA regulations. Physical Demands Summary: Requires lifting, bending and standing. Wage Rate: $11.25 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Q