    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36077": {
      "title": "Legal Research Assistant 1",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Legal Research Assistant 1 - Health Lab Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Legal Research Assistant 1 - Health Lab Associate To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260341V Position Title: Legal Research Assistant 1 - Health Lab Associate Posting Type Student Hours/week: No more than 20 hours/week during Spring and Fall; no more than 40 hours/week in Summer Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Widger Law School Building Detailed Work Schedule varies by student schedule Number of positions: varies Department: 241-Law School Instruction Contact Name: Cheryl Baro Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7003 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Legal Research Assistants (RAs) provide valuable research support for law faculty scholarship. In-depth and sophisticated legal and non-legal research, Analyzing various primary sources including state and federal statutes, caselaw, regulations, constitutions, and secondary legal sources such as law review articles and legal treatises, Communicating research results to faculty verbally and/or in writing, Comprehensive cite checking which requires an understanding of sources from full or partial citations and extensive knowledge and application of The Bluebook: A Uniform System of Citation, Maintaining confidentially of faculty projects and course assignments, Following protocols for academic legal writing regarding proper attribution, plagiarism, and general academic integrity, Working independently without daily supervision; exercising professional judgment when consulting with professor, librarians, and law school staff, Managing time and adhering to time sensitive deadlines, Acquiring and maintaining knowledge of any database or software necessary to support faculty research; examples include Zotero, Juris-M, Endnote, Microsoft Word (footnotes, tables of authorities, complex formatting), complex docket searching and data coding. Requirements: Must be hired by Professor Ana Santos Rutschman to assist with her health law research. Must be a currently enrolled law student at Villanova University’s Charles Widger School of Law. Additional Information: Please click the “Apply to this Job” link at the top of the page and submit the information requested in the application. Please use your permanent address. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
