    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35356": {
      "title": "Teacher",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Teacher Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Teacher To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Special Message to Applicants: Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu. Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae / Resume Names and contacts of three references Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20250660T Position Title: Teacher Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week 5 to 10 hours per week Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Position Summary: Villanova University, in collaboration with the North Penn School District, is launching an Afterschool Artificial Intelligence (AI) Club at local elementary schools as part of an NSF -supported outreach initiative. The program will bring together K–12 teachers, engineering students, and AI professionals to mentor elementary students (grades 1–6) as they explore how AI can be used to solve real-world challenges. The club will run January 2026 – June 2026, meeting two to three afternoons per week after school in Lansdale, PA. We are seeking K–12 teachers to serve as mentors and facilitators for the Afterschool AI Club. Teacher mentors will work alongside Villanova faculty and AI experts to plan and co-lead engaging, age-appropriate learning activities. They will play a critical role in supporting student teams as they develop creative AI-enabled projects for submission to the Presidential AI Challenge. This position offers teachers an opportunity to gain exposure to AI education, collaborate with university and industry mentors, and help shape an innovative STEM learning experience that integrates technology, creativity, and ethics. This is a part-time, hourly position (approximately 5–10 hours per week, January 2026 – June 2026). Looking to hire up to 2 individuals. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Co-develop and facilitate after-school AI Club sessions (two to three afternoons per week). Collaborate with Villanova faculty and AI experts to adapt materials for age-appropriate learning. Provide classroom management and guidance to maintain a positive, inclusive learning environment. Support student teams in project planning, documentation, and presentation development. Participate in planning and reflection meetings with mentors and the PI. Assist with the organization of a local AI Showcase and related outreach events. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Work Experience Current K–12 teacher in the North Penn School District or surrounding area. Demonstrated experience in lesson planning, classroom management, and student engagement. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Other : Availability for afterschool hours (typically between 3:00 and 6:00 p.m.) two to three days per week. Preferred Qualifications: Work Experience Experience in after-school or enrichment program facilitation. Other Interest in STEM or technology integration in the classroom. Openness to learning about Artificial Intelligence and integrating related concepts into teaching practice. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Availability for afterschool hours (typically between 3:00 and 6:00 p.m.) two to three days per week. Special Message to Applicants: Special Message to Applicants: Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu. Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae / Resume Names and contacts of three references EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 12/16/2025 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $30.93-32.64 per hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
