    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35923": {
      "title": "Export Control Analyst",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Export Control Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Export Control Analyst To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260388S Position Title: Export Control Analyst Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 919 - Office of Research and Graduate Programs Position Summary: The Export Control Analyst supports institutional compliance with U.S. export control laws and regulations, including the Export Administration Regulations ( EAR ), the International Traffic in Arms Regulations ( ITAR ), and the Office of Foreign Assets Control ( OFAC ) sanctions programs. Reporting to the Director of Research Security and Export Controls, this position manages Restricted Party Screening ( RPS ), develops and maintains Technology Control Plans (TCPs), monitors procurements, conducts commodity classifications, and contributes to the University’s broader research security efforts. The Export Control Analyst collaborates closely with faculty, research administrators, procurement, the Office of General Counsel, Offices of Research Administration, Public Safety, and University Technology Services to ensure full compliance with all applicable federal export control requirements. Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Manage and administer the University’s Restricted Party Screening ( RPS ) program, including screening of international collaborators, visitors, vendors, and other third parties against applicable federal denied and restricted party lists. Develop, maintain, and refine standard operating procedures for RPS workflows. Investigate and resolve potential screening matches and provide training and guidance to University personnel on RPS requirements. Draft, implement, and maintain Technology Control Plans (TCPs) for research projects involving export-controlled information, technology, or items. Collaborate with principal investigators, department chairs, IT security, and Facilities Management to develop tailored TCP requirements. Conduct periodic reviews and audits of active TCPs and maintain a central repository of all TCPs and associated documentation. Support the review of procurement transactions involving international shipments, deemed export risks, and the acquisition of controlled commodities, software, or technology. Perform and document commodity classifications and jurisdiction determinations ( EAR / ITAR ). Advise procurement, shipping, and receiving personnel on export control requirements and monitor evolving regulatory changes. Maintain accurate and organized records of all export control and research security activities. Support the Director of Research Security and Export Controls in preparing, reviewing, and submitting export license applications to BIS , DDTC , and OFAC . Assist in evaluating the applicability of license exceptions ( EAR ) and exemptions ( ITAR ). Maintain organized records of all license applications, exemption analyses, and related correspondence. Prepare materials and reports for internal and external audits, regulatory inquiries, and institutional leadership briefings. Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of export control policies, procedures, and compliance infrastructure. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree required. Candidates possessing a high-school diploma or GED may be considered with sufficient experience in export controls and research security related positions. Work Experience Minimum 2 years of experience in export control compliance, research compliance, trade compliance, or a closely related regulatory compliance field. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills ) Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate regulatory requirements clearly to non-specialist audiences. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships at all levels of the campus hierarchy. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Demonstrated working knowledge of the Export Administration Regulations ( EAR ), International Traffic in Arms Regulations ( ITAR ), and OFAC sanctions programs. Experience conducting restricted party screening using Visual Compliance, OCR Solutions, or similar screening platforms. Strong familiarity with commodity classification processes and jurisdiction determinations under the EAR and ITAR . Equipment Knowledge Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, screening platforms (such as Visual Compliance), and the ability to learn and effectively utilize compliance management software and databases. Other: Ability to exercise sound independent judgment and discretion when handling sensitive or confidential information. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Professional certification in export control or trade compliance (e.g., CECE from ACEP , or Export Compliance Professional ECoP® EAR / ITAR Certified). Work Experience Experience in a higher education or research institution. Experience developing and implementing Technology Control Plans in a university or research laboratory environment. Experience with federal sponsored research administration, including familiarity with award terms and conditions from agencies such as DoD, DOE , NSF , and NIH . Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Familiarity with NSPM -33 implementation guidance, the CHIPS and Science Act research security provisions, and related federal research security requirements. Knowledge of Controlled Unclassified Information ( CUI ) handling requirements and NIST SP 800-171 compliance frameworks. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: a.) Tools, machinery and equipment used: Standard office equipment including computer, telephone, printer. Compliance management software and restricted party screening platforms. b.) Environmental conditions: Standard office environment. No unusual or adverse conditions. Physical requirements: Standard office environment. Occasional travel may be available for professional development, training conferences, or regulatory meetings. Hybrid/flexible work arrangements may be available in accordance with University policy. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/04/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 16 and the range is $73,100-91,400. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 16 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31110": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science will start reviewing applications on February 1, 2024, but will keep accepting applications until the position is filled. The target starting date is June 1, 2024, with the possibility of shifting to both earlier and later dates, depending on the applicant needs/availability. All applicants must apply online and complete a faculty profile. Applications must include: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. A research statement. A statement of commitment to the principles of diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI). Two letters of recommendation; the system will request the letters directly from the references when appropriate in the process. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documentation, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20231096F Position Title: Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 182-Astronomy and Planetary Science Position Summary: Villanova University’s Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science invites applications for the NSF -sponsored postdoctoral research fellowship. A successful applicant will join Andrej Prsa’s research team and work on the PHOEBE code , advancing our understanding of the processes in contact binary stars. In parallel, the applicant will be given an opportunity to teach an undergraduate core science course/lab, where the stress is on incorporating four critical components in a meaningful way: problem solving, laboratory experience, technology and quantitative tools, and interdisciplinary understanding. While the teaching component is entirely optional, it is offered to provide development and growth in the applicant’s teaching. Finally, the applicant will join the Departmental ecosphere and participate in shaping the future of research and education at Villanova. The fellowship includes a 12-month salary, a travel budget and full employee benefits. The postdoctoral fellowship is a 3-year appointment, renewed annually under the condition of satisfactory performance and continued mutual interest. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: A successful applicant will be expected to: demonstrate the highest regard for the diverse, equitable and inclusive Departmental culture and uphold the true and complete respect for all students, staff and faculty; work with PHOEBE developers and contribute significantly to the PHOEBE code base and to the organization of PHOEBE summer workshops; focus on the state-of-the-art research in contact binary physics, namely the flow of mass and energy across the common envelope and the consequent dynamical equilibrium processes; work on formulating an atmosphere model for contact binary stars; partake in research that connects theoretical models and observational data from space-borne missions (most notably Kepler and TESS ); be proficient in computational astrophysics, astrostatistics, and/or exoplanetary science; participate in Departmental affairs: meetings, colloquia, events and functions. This includes working with and counseling undergraduate students, contributing to public events and advancing the Department’s reputation and renown locally, nationally and internationally; ( optional ) teach 1 or 2 sections of the core science courses or labs per semester (currently “How old is the Universe?”, “Life in the Universe”, “Planetary skies and landscapes”, “Birth and Death of Stars”, “Earth – our habitable world”, and “Earth – a cosmic connection”). Minimum Qualifications: A PhD in Physics, Astrophysics, Data Science or a closely related discipline is required. Strong proficiency with programming, especially in python and optionally in C/C++. Strict adherence to open source software and open science models. Ability and willingness to work as part of a large development team. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching : prior experience in teaching STEM classes to non- STEM majors is desired. Research : strong track record in physics, astrophysics, statistics and programming is desired. Service : ability to work with colleagues and to demonstrate diversity awareness is desired. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science will start reviewing applications on February 1, 2024, but will keep accepting applications until the position is filled. The target starting date is June 1, 2024, with the possibility of shifting to both earlier and later dates, depending on the applicant needs/availability. All applicants must apply online and complete a faculty profile. Applications must include: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. A research statement. A statement of commitment to the principles of diversity, equity and inclusion ( DEI ). Two letters of recommendation; the system will request the letters directly from the references when appropriate in the process. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documentation, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * What science field is your PhD in? Physics Astrophysics Computer/Data science Mathematics/Statistics Closely related field * If your answer above was a \"Closely related field,\" please provide it here. (Open Ended Question) * What programming experience and computing infrastructure background do you have? Select all that apply. C/C++/C# Python Java/Javascript HTML and web deployment IDL Bash scripting HPC/MPI environments Virtual reality visualization (vizard, unity, ...) Linux operating system Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Interests Statement of Contribution to DEI Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
