      "title": "Catering Bartender",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Catering Bartender Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Catering Bartender To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedule varies based on the needs of the department and various catering functions. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20200292T Position Title: Catering Bartender Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 423-Catering Position Summary: The Catering Bartenders are responsible for proper table/bar set-up, table service for guests, and knowledge of menu/drinks to be served. This person will apply all safe food/alcohol handling principles as they pertain to this position. This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Cleanliness and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Duties and Responsibilities: Set-up of dining room/bars for service. Taking customers orders and filling the order in a friendly and professional manner. Maintain a clean and neat work and service area. Performs clean up and breaking down of bars at end of event. Perform additional duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Bartending skills and practices. Oral and written communication skills. Ability to work independently as well as in a group under general supervision. Excellent customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications: Previous catering, serving or bartending experience. Ramp certification preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Ability to use various chemicals. Ability to sit/stand for extended periods. Ability to lift, push, pull up to 30 lbs independently. Special Message to Applicants: Schedule varies based on the needs of the department and various catering functions. EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 07/22/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $25.00/hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    80