    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34133": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Graduate Research Assistant - Data Analyst: Migration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Graduate Research Assistant - Data Analyst: Migration To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255395V Position Title: Graduate Research Assistant - Data Analyst: Migration Posting Type Graduate Assistant Hours/week: 8-10 hours/week Eligibility: Graduate Assistant Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Widger Law School Building Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 241-Law School Instruction Contact Name: Robyn Lieberman Contact Phone/Extension: 415-730-0416 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Summary and Information Job Description: The Mother Cabrini Institute on Immigration is working on a research project to identify and scale innovative models in immigration legal services, including building the enabling environment to expand the Department of Justice-Recognized Organization and Accredited Representatives program (“R+A”). In 2024, the SIG partnered with the Center for Migration Studies of New York to launch the first-ever national study of the R+A practitioners. We are currently looking for support from a data analyst to work with a senior researcher to clean/recode data files from two Qualtrics surveys and create data visualizations of the recoded data files. Before accessing the data, the research assistant will take CITI training (about 3-5 hours) or have existing IRB clearances. The position is virtual – you do not need to work from campus. Timeline: The research team projects 10-30 hours of week over 3-6 weeks in July and August 2025. Salary : The data analyst will be a Graduate Research Assistant for the Strategic Initiative for Migrants and Refugees, compensated at $18/hour. To apply: Submit a resume/CV and sample data cleaning/recoding code in Stata with your application. Must be a Villanova student. Requirements: Requirements: · Experience using Stata to clean and recode raw survey data, and to produce tables, figures, and other visualizations. · Experience producing maps using ArcGIS or other statistical mapping platforms is a plus. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $18/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35558": {
      "title": "STOVS-Program Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | STOVS-Program Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us STOVS-Program Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260037T Position Title: STOVS-Program Assistant Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week 49 for 3 weeks Monday - Sunday Department: 702 - Center for Access Success and Achievement Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . STOVS Program Assistant will assist with the program development, implementation and execution of the STOVS program. This position provides administrative support to the STOVS Program Director. Program is 35 hours/week for two weeks Duties and Responsibilities: Provide assistance to students and Program Coordinator (Monday- Friday 9:00am – 3pm)) Coordinate student activities and preparation for STOVS . Assist students in study hall through one-on-one mentoring (Mon-Fri afternoons between 3:00-5:30 p.m.). Meet with students to discuss goal-setting, healthy habits, and academic confidence. Assist with evening social and learning activities to maximize student engagement (Mon-Fri afternoons between 6:30-9:30 p.m.). Offer support to students who are struggling with course work, or who need assistance with their acclimation to Villanova. Attend and participate in planning and feedback meetings. Provide updates to STOVS director and professors regarding student concerns and needs. Be available for student questions and concerns via email throughout the program. Assist with program design. Assist with coordinating and scheduling of program and presenters. Assist with student paperwork/applications. Assist with all follow-up to students and their families. Facilitate group workshops and provide student advising weekly. Assist with with weekend activities and planning. Assist with Peer Leader supervision and other administrative tasks to be assigned. Be available for any student and parent questions and concerns via email throughout the program. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Advanced knowledge of student development theory. Ability to provide supportive and constructive feedback to students. Knowledge of issues of difference in higher education, particularly educational equity. Proven ability to use MS Office Suite and Adobe Acrobat. Work Skills: Excellent interpersonal skills to relate easily & effectively with students and staff. Possess traits of good judgment and maturity that align with the University’s mission. Will be required to work evenings throughout the duration of the program. Employment subject to satisfactory background check. Specific Job Knowledge: Proven ability to use MS Office Suite and Adobe Acrobat. Other: Will be required to work evenings throughout the duration of the program. Employment subject to satisfactory background check. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 07/02/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $15.00/hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36265": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Administrative Assistant II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Administrative Assistant II To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260246S Position Title: Administrative Assistant II Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 295-Office of Financial Assistance Position Summary: The Administrative Assistant II reports to the Director of Financial Assistance and is responsible for providing key administrative support for the Director and the Senior Associate Director of Financial Assistance. Other responsibilities include: monitoring vacation and sick records for Financial Assistance staff within the Banner system, assist in the management of the office operating budget, including preparation and submission of payment requests and monthly reconciliation of accounts, running and reviewing weekly reports to be distributed to counselors. This position maintains inventory and orders office supplies, equipment and forms for the office; serves as the primary contact to the Facilities Office for matters of repair or maintenance and performs all clerical duties for the Director (this includes the management of correspondence to and from the office). Responsible for scheduling and managing arrangements for financial aid related meetings with national, regional and state associations or organizations. This individual must participate in on-going training pertaining to all Federal, State and Institutionally funded programs as well as technical training necessary to keep up to date on the changes to software programs used by the office; responds to the needs of students, parents and others through in-person, telephone and e-mail contact and will be expected to answer questions pertaining to student aid eligibility, award status (e.g. disposition of aid to a student) and student billing account status; creation and updating of telephone/email scripts that are used in the office’s automated response system. Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Maintain calendar, schedule appointments, and perform clerical duties for Director and counselors including student appointments and scheduling of all on and off campus presentations, running and reviewing weekly reports for counselors. Maintain the Office Policy and Procedure Manual in paper and electronic format. Respond to the needs of students, parents and others through in-person, telephone and e-mail contact. Complete Sibling Enrollment Verification forms, scholarship forms and other documents requested by students for verification of their University aid. Manage Dropbox incoming documents. Manage & monitor department operating budget including the preparation of payment requests. Maintain inventory of office supplies, equipment & forms. Primary contact for all copy machine matters. Serve as primary contact with Facilities Management & Housekeeping. Prepare monthly reports on overtime hours of staff and the College Board Net Price Calculator Reports. Prepare the bi-weekly Enrollment Management update. Responsible for the preparation and circulation of the meeting minutes. Assist the Director and Counselors on other reports as needed. Maintain and monitor vacation and sick records, along with office calendar. Oversee the Office of Financial Assistance telephone/email script and serve as primary contact with University IT regarding all matters related to telephone/email. Participate in on-going training that will result in a mastery of information pertaining to all Federal, State and Institutionally funded programs of aid as well as training necessary to keep up to date on the changes to software necessary to perform all duties. Manage scheduling for financial-aid related meetings hosted by the University. Provide assistance to the Dean of Enrollment Management as needed Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education High school diploma required Work Experience Minimum 2 years of administrative assistant experience Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Excellent oral and written communication skills; strong organizational and interpersonal skills required. Ability to initiate and follow through with tasks as designated by the Director and outlined in this job description. Mastery of Microsoft Office. General knowledge of office principles and procedures is required. Basic principles of accounting and budget management. Equipment Knowledge Copiers; Personal Computer; Document Imager. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education · Some college and/or secretarial school experience preferred. Work Experience · Experience in higher education preferred. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) · Experience with Banner or similar Financial Aid System preferred. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 09/04/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 09/11/2026 Salary Posting Information: This position falls within hourly grade 11 and the range is $25.05-26.48/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 11 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
