    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35996": {
      "title": "Ticket Office Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Ticket Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Ticket Office Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260319V Position Title: Ticket Office Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Detailed Work Schedule Weeknight and weekend athletic events. Number of positions: 12 Department: 728-Athl - Ticket Office Contact Name: Eryn Schultz Contact Phone/Extension: eschul03@villanova.edu Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: In accordance with established policies and procedures, the Ticket Office Assistant provides exceptional customer service in person at the ticket office on game days for events hosted by Villanova Athletics. Answer customer inquiries and process ticket sales via walk-up orders. Responsible for daily reconciliation of ticket sales and payments. Other assignments may include but are not limited to the compliance pass entrance, will-call distribution and scanning operations. Perform other tasks as assigned by the Ticket Office staff. Requirements: Experience in an in-person customer service position. Familiarity with MS Office applications (Word/Excel). Applicants should be dependable, punctual and possess effective communication and problem solving skills, as well as strong attention to detail. Must have a customer-friendly personality and project a positive image of the University and the Athletics Department to fans, donors, staff, students, alumni, and other groups. Must be able to multi-task and work in a fast-paced environment. Must be able to work weeknights and weekends as needed for events, including working all home football games. Must have reliable transportation to and from athletic events. Additional Information: Athletic ticketed sports throughout the 2026- 2027 seasons include: Football, Volleyball, Women’s and Men’s Basketball, and Men’s and Women’s Lacrosse. 1-2 years customer service experience preferred but not required. Please attach a resume, cover letter and a copy of your VU Class Schedule. Physical Demands Summary: Some jobs require lifting, extensive walking and/or lengthy periods of standing along with exposure to both natural (i.e. weather) and event (i.e. music/crowd volume) related elements Wage Rate: $11.25 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * I understand that satisfactory attendance in all academic classes is required to maintain student employment at Villanova University. Yes No Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33249": {
      "title": "Director (Athletics Control Room)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Director (Athletics Control Room) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Director (Athletics Control Room) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20230509T Position Title: Director (Athletics Control Room) Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 732-Athletics - Promotion + Marketing Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University Athletics is now hiring highly motivated, skilled, and passionate director freelancers to join our Athletics Game Production team. The Director is responsible for the execution and implementation of all assets associated with the game production script at the direction of the Villanova Athletics Marketing/Operations staff and Athletics Building Engineer. The Director must have the expertise to execute full shows and be proficient with troubleshooting issues. All duties are to be performed in accordance with the department and venue policies and procedures. Duties and Responsibilities: Ensure all game production assets are implemented and executed in accordance with the game script. Assist Athletics Marketing/Operations staff will aspects of event production including but not limited to: owning and running pre-event coordination planning meetings, testing and rehearse elements as displayed in the event script, serve as primary point of contact for entire free-lance game staff, work in unison with Athletics Marketing/Operations staff and Athletics building engineer Have knowledge of technical operations including fundamentals of audio, video and graphics. Familiar with the language of a production control room and have a working knowledge of all current technology Ensure the safety of control room equipment at all times. Respect standards and regulations regarding the safety of equipment, and apply safe work methods. Provide support and assistance to other venue areas as needed Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned Minimum Qualifications: 3-5 years of related TD in live, multi-camera production preferred. Excellent interpersonal & communication skills required. Must be a collaborative team player who works well with others in a fast paced and dynamic environment. Available to work flexible hours including nights, weekends, and holidays Preferred Qualifications: Experience in the sports industry is ideal Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Available to work flexible hours including nights, weekends, and holidays Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 09/01/2023 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $500 per event (5hr crew call) Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tBasketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches?        Y         N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tCurrent VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes?    Y     N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
