    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34620": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Graduate Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Graduate Research Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260136V Position Title: Graduate Research Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 hours per week, during the academic year Eligibility: Graduate Assistant Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location St. Augustine Center Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 147-Theology/Religious Studies Contact Name: Michelle Maloney Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5246 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Support the Children, Liturgy, and Ecology Project being directed by Dr. Christy Lang Hearlson and Dr. Tim Brunk. Responsibilities will vary over time and will include some of the following: Support curriculum development through an ongoing lit review Plan local pilgrimage to a site of environmental interest Attend Symposium at Notre Dame, virtually or in person Help plan and support on-campus Symposium hosted by Villanova Lead or give support to (3) local pilgrimages to sites of environment interest (planned in the prior year) Support editorial process for book project Attend Grant-funded gatherings of congregational/parish leaders at Villanova Serve as coaches to congregational leaders developing projects Attend Grant-funded gatherings of congregational/parish leaders at Villanova Visit Philadelphia-area congregations to observe projects Requirements: -Current PhD Student in Theology and Religious Studies Department at Villanova -Must be able to transport themselves via car or public transportation to sites in and around Philadelphia -Must have access to a computer -Conscientious and capable of independent work -Capable of communicating professionally with community members and church leaders -Knowledgeable about or interested in the topics of children, liturgy/worship, and ecology/environmentalism Additional Information: These positions are for a semester at a time; ending no later than 31 August 2027. . Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $21 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
