    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35359": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20250609T Position Title: Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Periodically, as-needed Department: 733-Athletics - Training Room Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University Athletics has immediate opening for a temporary (fill-in) Athletic Trainer Certified ( ATC ). Under the license of our Team Physician, assist the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine in all activities related to the delivery of health-care to our varsity student-athletes (sports assigned by Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine), which includes working cooperatively and in conjunction with the Strength & Conditioning Staff. Design, implement and supervise appropriate treatment and rehabilitation programs for student-athletes, by maximizing and individualizing integrated training programs to achieve desired outcomes. Fill-in coverage for teams and events as needed. Perform all duties in compliance with all rules, regulations, and bylaws of the NCAA , associated Conferences, and University relating to the conduct and administration of the program. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsible for the coordination and supervision of the delivery of health care to assigned programs. Fill-in coverage as needed. Responsible for all phases of health care Design and implement treatment and rehab programs for time-loss and surgical rehab cases. Assist with the implementation of the Athletics Department Drug Testing Program Serve as a liaison between Sports Medicine staff and Strength & Conditioning staff regarding rehabilitation programs. Assist in the management of external accounts, including pharmacy and Physical therapy. Serving as liaison with the Health Center and outside medical practices associated with the care of varsity student athletes. Responsible for the daily electronic medical documentation for all student-athletes. Assist with the daily operation and maintenance of the athletic training facility. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned by the Director of Sports Medicine. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s Degree in sports medicine/athletic training or related field; current NATABOC certification; Pennsylvania Athletic Training Class A Certification required by start date. Current CPR / AED Certification. Minimum Work Experience At least 1 year athletic training experience including preventive, evaluative, and rehabilitative skills. Must have knowledge of health care insurance issues and drug testing protocols. Must have extensive experience with post-surgical rehabilitation. Experienced with therapeutic modalities and rehabilitative equipment. Ability to keep good records, including S.O.A.P. notes, daily rehab updates, and injury reports and proficiency with personal computer applications necessary. Excellent communication skills. Ability to demonstrate and instruct during rehab and functional training protocols. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with a variety of sports. Collegiate level experience a plus. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Available to work flexible hours including nights, weekends, and possible travel. Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 03/03/2025 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $40/hr. Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tBasketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches?        Y         N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tCurrent VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes?    Y     N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
