    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31113": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science will start reviewing applications on July 15, 2024. All applicants must apply online and complete a faculty profile. Applications must include: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. A research statement. A teaching statement. A statement of commitment to the principles of diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI). Two letters of recommendation, the system will request the letters directly from the references when appropriate in the process. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20241144F Position Title: Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 182-Astronomy and Planetary Science Position Summary: Villanova University’s Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science invites applications for the Mendel postdoctoral research fellowship. The Mendel fellowship is a flagship postdoctoral opportunity for candidates seeking to stay in academia. The fellowship provides training and development in all three areas of academic life: research, teaching, and service. A successful applicant will join Andrej Prsa’s research team and work on cutting-edge theoretical and observational aspects of binary and multiple stellar populations. In parallel, the applicant will teach an undergraduate core science course/lab to non- STEM majors, where the stress is on incorporating four critical components in a meaningful way: problem-solving, laboratory experience, technology and quantitative tools, and interdisciplinary understanding. Finally, the applicant will join the Departmental ecosphere and participate in shaping the future of research and education at Villanova. The Mendel postdoctoral fellowship is a 2-year appointment, with the possibility of extending it for another year. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: A successful applicant will be expected to: Demonstrate the highest regard for the diverse, equitable and inclusive Departmental culture and uphold the true and complete respect for all students, staff and faculty. Partake in state-of-the-art research in theoretical and observational stellar astrophysics, computation astrophysics, astrostatistics, and/or exoplanetary science. Teach 2 sections of the Mendel core science courses or labs per semester (currently “How old is the Universe?”, “Life in the Universe”, “Planetary skies and landscapes”, “Birth and Death of Stars”, “Earth – our habitable world”, and “Earth – a cosmic connection”). Participate in Departmental affairs: meetings, colloquia, events and functions. This includes working with and counseling undergraduate students, contributing to public events and advancing the Department’s reputation and renown locally, nationally and internationally. Minimum Qualifications: A PhD in Physics, Astrophysics, Data Science or a closely related discipline is required. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching : prior experience in teaching STEM classes to non- STEM majors is desired. Research : strong background in physics, astrophysics, statistics and programming is desired. Service : track record of the ability to work with others and to demonstrate diversity awareness is desired. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science will start reviewing applications on July 15, 2024. All applicants must apply online and complete a faculty profile. Applications must include: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. A research statement. A teaching statement. A statement of commitment to the principles of diversity, equity and inclusion ( DEI ). Two letters of recommendation, the system will request the letters directly from the references when appropriate in the process. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 07/10/2024 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) What science field is your PhD in? Physics Astrophysics Computer/Data science Mathematics/Statistics Closely related field If your answer above was a \"Closely related field,\" please provide it here. (Open Ended Question) What programming experience and computing infrastructure background do you have? Select all that apply. C/C++/C# Python Java/Javascript HTML and web deployment IDL Bash scripting HPC/MPI environments Virtual reality visualization (vizard, unity, ...) Linux operating system Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Interests Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Contribution to DEI Statement of Contribution to Mission Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35108": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include: A letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references) Current and complete curriculum vitae Statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260036F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology) Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 202-Civil and Environmental Engineering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. Even as a part-time employee, you will receive access to certain benefits, including tuition assistance and more . Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Civil and Environmental Engineering for graduate courses taught in the evening and/or undergraduate courses taught during the day. The Civil and Environmental Engineering Department offers programs leading to the B.S. and M.S. degrees and participates in the College of Engineering Ph.D. degree program. For this position, we are specifically looking for an adjunct faculty member to teach the graduate level course CEE 7511 Microbiology Environmental Engineering. The course description is as follows: Introduction to microbiology and biochemistry; bacteria, fungi, algae, protozoa, and viruses; structure, function, synthesis, and degradation of lipids, proteins, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates; nutritional requirements for microbial growth; waterborne disease; indicator organisms; microbial ecology; and microbiology of the nitrifiers, methanogens, and sulfur bacteria. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and other duties which vary with specific courses. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required. The applicant must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Civil Engineering or closely allied discipline is strongly preferred. Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Undergraduate courses are offered during the day; graduate courses during the evening. Graduate courses include a synchronous component. Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include: A letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references) Current and complete curriculum vitae Statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: 05/21/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35853": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Program Operations,  Doctoral Programs (PhD & DNP)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Director Program Operations,  Doctoral Programs (PhD &amp; DNP) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Director Program Operations,  Doctoral Programs (PhD & DNP) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260384S Position Title: Assistant Director Program Operations,  Doctoral Programs (PhD & DNP) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 232-Nursing Position Summary: The Assistant Director for Program Operations, Doctoral Programs (AD) provides high level administrative and operational support for the post-masters Doctor of Nursing Practice (non- DNP -NA) and Doctor of Philosophy programs, including directing and overseeing operations, logistics, communications, and adherence to University policies. The AD collaborates with program leadership and faculty, to implement, monitor, evaluate, and revise graduate policies, processes, and resources. The AD advances operational excellence of doctoral nursing education, the student experience, and all business operations in accordance with the University and FCN mission and strategic plan. Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Student Support Serves as the primary point of contact for all programmatic questions and concerns. Maintains the schedule for Doctoral programs including, but not limited to, on-campus residencies, Research Colloquium and DNP Scholary Projects presentations. Completes initial registration for all new students and resolves all registration concerns. Communicates and supports students with processing Nurse Faculty Loan Program ( NFLP ) applications and accessing financial aid. Updates plans of study and tracks/documents progress for in-coming and returning cohorts. Collaborates with marketing and communication team to communicate student accomplishments. Maintains all program and student records. Serves as primary point of contact for doctoral students for program related questions, processes, and resources and faciliates resolution of student concerns and needs. Provides faculty with necessary materials, for advisement and other academic-related issues. Coordinates and facilitates new student program orientation in collaboration with the program directors.. Works collaboratively with the Assistant Director, Graduate Program Operations to facilitate access to financial aid and scholarships available through the University and College. Data Management Activities Gathers and analyzes data to assess progress toward program goals. Provides reliable program specific data to satisfy reporting requirements of relevant agencies for compliance, accrediation, and rankings. Creates, updates, and distributes online surveys to obtain feedback for the Doctoral Programs that contribute to the College’s Program Evaluation Plan ( PEP ). Supports management of application enrollments and student progression data using the University’s student application and enrollment software system (Slate). Maintains records of deliberations and scores to ensure transparent, equitable, and effective review process. Collaborates with the Recruitment and Enrollment team using the CRM ( SLATE ) and other University software systems to generate and analyze program data to optimize enrollment. In collaboration with Program Directors, develops a plan for the schedule of courses, makes adjustments to meet program needs, and ensures the timely submission of data to the Associate Dean of Graduate Programs and Assistant Director, Graduate Program Operations to satisfy deadlines set by the Office of the Registrar. Tracks and maintains records of current and historical scholarships for the Doctoral Programs. Coordinates end of program activites and submits required graduation data to the Office of the Registrar and/or other university entities related to graduation. Works closely with the Office of Financial Assistance to manage applications, distribution of funds, and satisfy all reporting requirements for NFLP . Reports activities and maintains the HRSA Electronic Handbook. General Office Administrative Duties Assists Program Directors to maintain calendars and appointments, and processes information requests and daily correspondence. Edits, copies and proofreads documents to support program operations. Coordinates all on campus and online logistics for doctoral programs including but not limited to, scheduling doctoral dissertation proposals, defenses, and scholarly project presentations. Coordinates all logistics for program events and activities in collaboration with the Dean’s Office. Maintains accuracy of all Clean Catalog materials related to the doctoral programs. Maintains essential program documents including alumni records, as well as completed dissertation and DNP scholarly project materials. Recruitment & Retention Collaborates with the Recruitment and Enrollment teams to ensure timely responses to prospective student inquiries. Participates in the doctoral program virtual information sessions, and other events. As a subject matter expert, contribute to developmnent and maintenance of recruitment and marketing materials including the doctoral program websites. General College wide activities Participates in college-wide activities, including but not limited to, convocation, graduation, and alumni mass. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum Work Experience 3+ years of relevant and applicable work experience in a professional environment. Direct experience in student support, academic advising and/or professional development at an institution of higher education, preferably at the graduate school level for both online and campus programs or comparable experience in an organization/corporation (preferably for remote and onsite employees). Experience coordinating and executing events onsite and virtually. Experience writing effective communications to students or employees for whom they are responsible for providing support and guidance on academic and/or professional development-related plans. Proven track record of providing excellent customer service and the ability to nurture relationships with various stakeholders. Work Skills Excellent written, oral communication, presentation, facilitation, interpersonal, and collaborative skills. Demonstrates professionalism and a strong commitment to teamwork. Strong organization skills, the ability to handle a fast-paced environment and manage multiple requests/projects/tasks with varied deadlines within timeframes required by the programs. Ability to manage competing priorities and meet multiple deadlines while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Results-oriented with ability to anticipate and identify problems and opportunities and take decisive action to proactively address them. Demonstrates poise and strong customer-service skills and the ability to work independently under general supervision. Ability to quickly learn and stay abreast of detailed curricular and program features in the degree portfolio. Ability to maintain confidentiality in all aspects of student, faculty, staff and agency information. Highly proficient or expert in all standard computer applications, including Microsoft Office products, particularly Microsoft Word, Powerpoint, Excel, online survey tools (Qualtrics), and the Teams application. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Understands and adheres to all relevant College and University policies and procedures. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree preferred. Experience supporting a doctoral/graduate office in a higher education institution Experience in a healthcare setting. Knowledge of Banner is a plus. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 07/28/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $51,000-63,800. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/30948": {
      "title": "Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university and the Mechanical Engineering faculty are internationally recognized for their research and teaching. The department has 23 full-time faculty members, approximately 300 undergraduate students, and 150 graduate students. We are committed to providing a rigorous educational experience in the discipline of mechanical engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. The Department of Mechanical Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. This commitment is realized in strong collaborative relationships between our department and faculty with the Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, the McNulty Institute for Women’s Leadership, and the VISIBLE (Villanova Initiative to Support Inclusiveness and Build Leaders) Office. The University is located 12 miles from Philadelphia along the historic Main Line. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. Please submit your applications at: http://jobs.villanova.edu. Application materials should include a cover letter, CV, transcript, teaching philosophy and the names of three references. The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2022895F Position Title: Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Position Summary: The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Villanova University has an opening for a full-time, continuing non tenure-track assistant professor position in the area of mechanics and materials. This is an academic year appointment, renewable subject to enrollment needs, availability of funding, and performance. The position starts in August 2022. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate core and laboratory courses in mechanical engineering, especially in the area of mechanics and materials. Other responsibilities include coordinating and maintaining course related laboratory equipment, mentoring undergraduate students, K-12 outreach, and developing new pedagogical methods. Minimum Qualifications: Requirements include a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field and a demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and innovation. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university and the Mechanical Engineering faculty are internationally recognized for their research and teaching. The department has 23 full-time faculty members, approximately 300 undergraduate students, and 150 graduate students. We are committed to providing a rigorous educational experience in the discipline of mechanical engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. The Department of Mechanical Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. This commitment is realized in strong collaborative relationships between our department and faculty with the Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, the McNulty Institute for Women’s Leadership, and the VISIBLE (Villanova Initiative to Support Inclusiveness and Build Leaders) Office. The University is located 12 miles from Philadelphia along the historic Main Line. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. Please submit your applications at: http://jobs.villanova.edu. Application materials should include a cover letter, CV, transcript, teaching philosophy and the names of three references. The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 01/31/2022 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
