    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34677": {
      "title": "Communication Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Communication Assistant - McNulty Institute Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Communication Assistant - McNulty Institute To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260141V Position Title: Communication Assistant - McNulty Institute Posting Type Student Hours/week: 5-8 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Tolentine Hall Detailed Work Schedule Flexible Number of positions: 1 Department: 938 – McNulty Institute Contact Name: Danielle Ross Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-6337 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Anne Welsh McNulty Institute for Women’s Leadership seeks a Student Communication Assistant to support its multiple communication initiatives. The position will support the Women’s Leadership Diaries platform, a multimedia series featuring individuals who are reshaping our perception and definition of leader through a lens of diverse women’s daily experience of leadership. Additionally, through the collection and analysis of stories, the communication assistant will contribute to future research focused on understanding the daily experiences of women leaders. Furthermore, the Communication Assistant will be a key influencer in the development of the Women’s Leadership Diaries through decision-making, contributing feedback, facilitating growth opportunities, and providing leadership to other McNulty Institute student communication assistants. Responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: Reviewing nominations and communicating with subjects to collect and write their stories for additions to the platform Curating content to be thematic and in line with the mission of the McNulty Institute Producing, editing, and posting blogs, podcasts, and videos through multimedia platforms Promoting WLD stories through social media platforms Taking initiative and bringing forth new and creative ideas to support the growth of the Women’s Leadership Diaries The position will also support the McNulty Institute’s social media and marketing efforts. Responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: Researching and generating fact sheets pertaining to women’s advancement and gender equity Designing templates to use for social media Supporting cross-campus partnerships through marketing initiatives General website updates Requirements: The candidate supporting the Women’s Leadership Diaries will have an interest in journalistic skills and experience, as well as editing and production skills related to blogs, podcasts, website development, and video production. The ideal candidate will have experience in multimedia communications and strong verbal and written communication skills. Candidates must be able to take initiative and multitask, and exhibit mature decision-making capabilities. Additionally, proven experience in creativity and innovation that will further the growth of the McNulty Institute’s communication initiatives is preferred. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $11.25/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample/Publications Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35752": {
      "title": "Information Technology Technician I",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260272V Position Title: Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support Posting Type Student Hours/week: 5 - 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Detailed Work Schedule Emphasis is placed on availability for the following shifts: M-F, 7:00 am – 10:00 am M-Th, 4:30 pm – 7:00 pm Sat, 8:30 am – 1:00 pm, as needed; Cabrini availability is highly valued. Transportation between campuses available based on Shuttle schedule. Other availability will be considered. Number of positions: 17 - 22 Department: 289-UTS - Classroom Technologies Contact Name: Evan Dorsey Contact Phone/Extension: x95219 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Learning Space Student Technicians are the main source of audiovisual assistance for professors and presenters in teaching and learning spaces. The main responsibilities of these technicians entail: Ensuring uninterrupted learning space operations by responding to hotline inquiries with immediate, high-priority phone and in-person support. Collaborating with full-time staff to deliver comprehensive technical support to faculty, staff, and the broader university community. Assessing, resolving, and documenting learning space service requests, incidents, and tasks within the ticketing system to ensure accurate records. Facilitating efficient setup and real-time support for learning space technology to keep academic schedules on track. Diagnosing and resolving hardware and software malfunctions during active instruction and between classes to minimize downtime. Ensuring long-term hardware reliability by maintaining accurate asset records and performing routine functional systems testing and preventive maintenance. Gaining hands-on experience with technical projects involving the deployment, maintenance, and optimization of specialized audiovisual software and hardware. Requirements: Preferred candidates will possess the following skills: Excellent written and oral communication skills, particularly in contexts of customer service; the ability to handle potentially challenging situations. Excellent interpersonal skills, specifically the ability to cultivate positive work relationships. Working knowledge of multimedia equipment operation and interfacing. Well-developed problem-solving skills. High degree of adaptability. Working knowledge of Windows, macOS, Zoom/Teams, and Microsoft 365. Knowledge of HTML5 highly valued. Training provided to ensure job success. Additional Information: The Learning Space Student Technician position comes with responsibilities and sometimes challenging situations, but it prepares students for life after college; it provides the skills, the professional training and the life lessons needed for internal advancement and future fulfilling employment. Exemplary student employees will be recognized and promoted within the team. In preparation for the opening of Cabrini Campus, ATS is increasing its student staff, presenting more opportunities for student employment. This position is technical but not exclusive; students of all majors are welcome to apply. ATS is currently interviewing primarily for Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 ATS focuses on fostering a welcoming work environment where student employees are treated with kindness, dignity, and respect. Physical Demands Summary: Should be able to efficiently walk the campus and carry a laptop. Exceptions and accommodations will be considered on a case by case basis for individuals with documented needs. Lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, etc. Wage Rate: $11.25 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36093": {
      "title": "Director of Professional Development and Leadership",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Director of Professional Development and Leadership Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Director of Professional Development and Leadership To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260405S Position Title: Director of Professional Development and Leadership Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 241-Law School Instruction Position Summary: Reporting to the Associate Dean for Professional Development and Leadership, the Director of Professional Development and Leadership plays a central role in preparing law students for successful, fulfilling careers. As a highly visible member of the Law School’s Professional Development team, this position combines classroom teaching and innovative program development to help students build the professional competencies and leadership skills essential to thrive in the legal profession. Working collaboratively with the Associate Dean and Faculty Director, the Director designs, teaches, and continuously enhances the Law School’s comprehensive Professional Development curriculum and related programming. Through frequent and meaningful engagement with students, the Director delivers workshops, facilitates learning opportunities, and supports students in developing a strong professional identity grounded in the values, ethics, judgment, and responsibilities of the legal profession. The Director plays a key role in fostering students’ professional identity formation, helping them connect their personal values and strengths with the competencies and expectations of the legal profession while preparing them to navigate an evolving legal landscape with confidence and integrity. This role offers the opportunity to make a lasting impact on students’ academic experience, professional identity formation, and long-term success as lawyers and leaders. Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Plan, implement, and facilitate the Professional Development curriculum and related programming, including leadership programming, under the strategic guidance of the Associate Dean for Professional Development and Leadership and the Faculty Director. Collaborate with faculty to infuse professional development concepts into academic curriculum. Cultivate student leadership of and involvement in professional development programming. Coordinate with the Office of Career Strategy and Advancement, the Director of Experiential Learning, faculty advisors, alumni, and employers with respect to the Professional Development and leadership curriculum. Identify and implement additional opportunities to integrate professional development and leadership programming throughout the Law School experience. Review and evaluate student work. Prepare and enhance student tools for self-assessment and professional development, including integration of assessment tools into the curriculum. Create and implement opportunities for customization and individualization within the Professional Development curriculum, including programming for students who are planning a career outside of the traditional practice of law. Provide advising and programming on professional development matters, which may include the following: counseling students on career and professional development concerns and planning, implementing, and facilitating programming and communication strategies for first generation, underrepresented, and diverse students. Assist in seeking ways to enhance professional development and employment outcomes for all students. Represent the Law School to the legal employment community and at related bar association events and other conferences. Keep current on lawyer education, professional development, and employment trends. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. 5 years legal work experience or experience in attorney, professional, or student professional development required. Demonstrated leadership skills. Superior research, organization, written and oral communication skills (including public speaking). Counseling, listening, and empathy skills. Commitment to inclusion. Close attention to detail and procedures. Ability to work effectively with technology. Ability to work effectively with a variety of people and constituencies. Ability to prioritize, multi-task, approach challenges with creativity, insight and resourcefulness. Able to work independently, demonstrate initiative, effectively balance multiple tasks simultaneously, and to be part of a diverse and collegial team. Willingness to occasionally travel. Substantial knowledge of, and experience with, professional development and/or legal practice. A vision for how the Law School can provide the highest quality professional development program for students and alumni. Counseling, mentoring, training, and multicultural competence. Networking and marketing skills. Essential office technology applications, including MS Word, calendar programs, e-mail, voice mail, etc. Preferred Qualifications: JD preferred. Prior experience and/or training in legal education, counseling, mentoring and inclusion matters preferred. Experience with Excel or comparable databases as well as 12Twenty and SCT Banner software is desirable. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Moderate physical exertion required at times, including lifting, standing or sitting for extended periods, pushing / pulling, manual dexterity (for computers, etc.), travel and associated exertion. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/20/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 16 and the range is $73,100-91,400. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 16 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33406": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Studio Art Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Studio Art To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Theatre and Studio Art Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; © The names and contact information for 3 references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2019625F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Studio Art Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 146-Theatre Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Studio Art for undergraduate courses only. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester but may include Basic Drawing and Basic Watercolor Painting, among others. The applicant must be committed to excellence in the teaching of communication. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: An MFA in a visual arts discipline is required and/or experience suitable for course instruction. Preferred Qualifications: Previous undergraduate teaching experience strongly preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Night classes are possible (6:10-8:50 pm). Special Message to Applicants: The Theatre and Studio Art Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; © The names and contact information for 3 references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 07/16/2019 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
