    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36157": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260413S Position Title: Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 654 - University Communications and Marketing - Advancement Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . In close collaboration with the Director, University Advancement Communication, and as a member of the University Advancement Communication ( UAC )leadership team, the Assistant Director of University Advancement Communication is responsible for leading the execution of creative and integrated multi-channel advancement communications for the full spectrum of University fundraising, stewardship and engagement activities across a wide variety of constituencies and donor levels. This includes working with University Advancement staff across campus to oversee a portfolio of advancement communication projects in their assigned University Advancement (UA) areas, including Alumni Relations, Stewardship, Family Engagement and Philanthropy, and Corporate and Foundation Relations, among others. It also includes working closely with the Director to ensure the effective and efficient operation of the UAC department. The Assistant Director manages one Communication Associate, providing day-to-day project support and direction, as well as helping to ensure their projects meet the University’s advancement and strategic goals. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: In close collaboration with the Director, and as a member of the UAC leadership team, the Assistant Director, UAC , is responsible for leading the execution of creative and integrated multi-channel advancement communications for University Advancement. Plans, prioritizes and oversees a portfolio of advancement communication projects in their respective UA areas while building and strengthening relationships with advancement staff across campus, and serves as a leader to support overall advancement communication goals. Manages one Communication Associate in all aspects of project management for a wide range of advancement communication projects to ensure excellence and the successful implementation, coordination and completion of all deadlines, as well as ensuring that advancement and strategic goals are met. The Assistant Director, UAC , will supervise these daily activities, goal setting and overall performance, providing project assistance, guidance, feedback and support. The Assistant Director, UAC , also works closely with the Director to ensure the efficiency and effectiveness of departmental operations, including all project management and communication systems are running to deliver projects on deadline and on budget. Performs other duties and assists with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications or a related field required, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Work Experience Must have 5+ years of relevant communication and marketing experience within an academic, non-profit or business environment. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) This individual must be a team player with strong writing, research, interpersonal, management, organizational and planning skills. Must be a flexible self-starter who enjoys collaboration with a wide variety of constituencies. Must have excellent written and verbal communication, problem solving and decision making skills with the ability to build and maintain excellent internal and external relationships. Must have the ability to handle multiple projects, priorities and deadlines within a fast-paced, multifaceted environment with the ability to work evenings, weekends and possibly holidays as the demands of the job dictates. Must be able to handle confidential information with a high level of discretion. This individual must have a deep commitment to the well-being of the University, a commitment to the University’s Augustinian Catholic heritage, the advancement of its mission and to serving the needs of a diverse community. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) This individual must have a broad working knowledge of communication and marketing with a proven record of developing, leading. executing and assessing strategic and tactical marketing and communications plans. Must be highly proficient in all standard computer applications, including Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Adobe Acrobat. Equipment Knowledge Personal computers, copiers and other standard office equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Experience with direct mail, and/or fundraising and alumni communication is strongly preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Must have the ability to work evenings, weekends and possibly holidays as the demands of the job dictates. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/26/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 16 and the range is $71,700-89,600. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 16 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33424": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include the contact information for 3 references who will be contacted for finalists only. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2021804F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 133-Classical Studies Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Classical Studies for undergraduate and/or graduate (M.A.) courses. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester (e.g., Latin and/or ancient Greek language at all levels, Latin and/or ancient Greek literature, Greek and/or Roman history/culture). The applicant must be committed to excellence in teaching. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Graduate (M.A.) courses will be taught either online or simulcast (campus and online). Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have an M.A. in Classics and be working towards a Ph.D. in Classics or related field. Candidates must have teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Classics. For graduate (M.A.) courses, experience teaching online. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include the contact information for 3 references who will be contacted for finalists only. Posting Date: 06/22/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Summary of Teaching Evaluations Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610)