    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35595": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Postdoctoral Researcher - Electrical and Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Postdoctoral Researcher - Electrical and Computer Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering is committed to providing rigorous educational experience in the discipline of Electrical and Computer Engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. Please submit your application at: https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Application packages must include : Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Statements on Teaching Philosophy One representative publication / paper Names and contact information of two references Note : The successful candidate will be required to submit a Statement of Contribution to University Mission The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260054F Position Title: Postdoctoral Researcher - Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will actively contribute to project objectives, collaborate with members of the research team, and support the research program led by Dr. Mojtaba Vaezi. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The postdoctoral researcher is expected to actively contribute to the project, work collaboratively as part of the research team, and perform the following major tasks: Conduct theoretical analysis, algorithm development, and simulation studies in the area of machine learning for wireless communications. Develop and implement machine learning techniques for communication systems, with a strong emphasis on producing high-quality research outcomes. Publish research findings in leading journals and conferences and contribute to the dissemination of project results. Assist the PI in preparing manuscripts, presentations, and research proposals. Participate in weekly research meetings and contribute to project reports and presentations for the project sponsor. Collaborate with graduate students and other researchers involved in the project and contribute to a productive and innovative research environment. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a closely related field. Strong organizational, written, and oral communication skills. Ability to work independently and communicate proactively and effectively within a research team. Highly motivated with a strong work ethic and passion for research. Research experience in wireless communications, signal processing, information theory, or related areas. Preferred Qualifications: Research experience in machine learning for wireless communications, with particular emphasis on interference management and channel coding. Strong publication record or demonstrated potential for publishing in leading journals and conferences. Demonstrated ability and motivation to pursue high-impact research, generate new ideas, and contribute to proposal development and scientific writing. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering is committed to providing rigorous educational experience in the discipline of Electrical and Computer Engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. Please submit your application at: https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Application packages must include : Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Statements on Teaching Philosophy One representative publication / paper Names and contact information of two references Note : The successful candidate will be required to submit a Statement of Contribution to University Mission The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 07/08/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Writing Sample/Publications Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
