    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33443": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor - Global Interdisciplinary Studies (Scholar and Field Expert Lecturer) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Instructor - Global Interdisciplinary Studies (Scholar and Field Expert Lecturer) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest that includes the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20241176F Position Title: Adjunct Instructor - Global Interdisciplinary Studies (Scholar and Field Expert Lecturer) Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 317-Dept of Global Interdisciplinary Studies Position Summary: The Global Interdisciplinary Studies Department will accept applications for the two-week visiting instructorship in our Scholar-and-Field-Expert Lecture Series. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest that includes the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties over two weekends for a total of 12 hours of instruction. Minimum Qualifications: Advanced degrees in the social sciences, humanities, law, or or a closely related discipline is required and/or experience suitable for course instruction. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in public policy design and implementation, advocacy Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest that includes the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 10/14/2024 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34777": {
      "title": "Receiving Clerk",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Receiving Clerk - Donahue Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Receiving Clerk - Donahue To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours Tuesday - Saturday 6am - 3pm Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260176S Position Title: Receiving Clerk - Donahue Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 412-Dining Services Operations Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Receiving Clerk is responsible for receiving and recording in all food products, supplies, and merchandise. The individual in this position must keep accurate record of inventory on hand, used and ordered. The Receiving Clerk is also the delivery driver as needed for on campus drop-offs. This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Inspect, receive, and record all food and supplies delivered according to safe food handling guidelines and procedures. Responsible for returning and refusing items. Date and store all food and supplies according to safe food handling guidelines and procedures utilizing the FIFO system of inventory. Maintain accurate inventory records of all food products, supplies, and merchandise entered into the building. Maintain order and cleanliness of all food and non-food storage areas. Drives University Vehicles for Dining Services as needed. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High School degree or equivalent. Work Experience: 1+ year as a receiver or related experience dealing with inventory control. Work Skills: Must possess math skills to keep records of inventory on hand, used, and ordered. Must possess a valid driver’s license and must be an approved University driver in accordance with the University’s motor vehicle record policy for drivers. Must be able to follow directions and complete assigned tasks. Must have basic and effective communication skills and basic reading and writing skills. Must be able to work with minimal supervision and follow directions and complete assigned tasks. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: Kitchen Equipment Environmental conditions: Ability to use chemicals daily and use proper protective equipment as called for by the specific chemical and task. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift, push, pull up to 50 lbs independently. Ability to withstand extreme temperatures (hot/cold). Ability to use chemicals. Special Message to Applicants: SCHEDULE during normal operating hours Tuesday – Saturday 6am – 3pm Posting Date: 04/25/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98 an hour shift differential added for qualifying shifts Salary Grade: 10 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
