    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36110": {
      "title": "Facilities Attendants and Aides- Athletics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Facilities Attendants and Aides- Athletics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Facilities Attendants and Aides- Athletics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260347V Position Title: Facilities Attendants and Aides- Athletics Posting Type Student Hours/week: up to 20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Finneran Pavilion Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 10 Department: 730-Athl - The Pavilion Contact Name: Dominik Barczak Contact Phone/Extension: 215-687-9357 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Assists in the operations of the facility including game preparation and set up, facilitate game operations, data entry, filing, mailings, and other duties as assigned. Requirements: Training available, but experience is preferred. Evening and weekend hours are constant throughout the year and are a major requirement for employment Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Lift 50 pounds. Wage Rate: $10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant