    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35419": {
      "title": "Access Services Night Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Access Services Night Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Access Services Night Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260243V Position Title: Access Services Night Manager Posting Type Student Hours/week: 8.5 -15 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Falvey Memorial Library Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 2 Department: 288-Falvey Library Contact Name: Lorraine Holt Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-4291 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Access Services Night Managers provide supervisory support to the Access Services department of Falvey Library. Night Managers are responsible for conducting the following tasks and procedures: Manage library desk services independently during late night hours (Sunday – Thursday) and weekend hours. Supervise and manage undergraduate student desk staff. Conduct circulation services, including supervisor policy overrides as needed. Provide basic to intermediate research assistance; conduct and interpret library catalog searches; refer patrons to subject librarian research services. Acquire and maintain knowledge of library policies; make informed decisions based on library policies, precedents, and operations. Assist with holds and interlibrary loan processing. Conduct additional library tasks as assigned. Assist patrons with library technology. Maintain and troubleshoot public printers, microfilm scanners, and book scanner technology. Maintain and troubleshoot service desk computers and technology. Assist patrons with computer hardware and software problems; refer patrons to UTS as needed. Respond to patron complaints and library disruptions, contact Public Safety and Access Services staff as needed. Report desk activities, situations, and issues that require follow-up to Service Desk Coordinators or appropriate Access Services staff. Conduct closing procedures: secure library collections and materials, shut down and secure department areas, conduct preliminary closing walkthroughs, contact Public Safety for final closing walkthroughs. Contact Public Safety for facilities, custodial, and emergency services, such as building maintenance or safety concerns. Requirements: Must be a currently enrolled graduate student at Villanova University . Excellent verbal and written communication skills; strict attention to detail and reliability are required. Ability to work and make decisions independently required. Ability to perform repetitive tasks with great accuracy and consistency required. Excellent interpersonal skills; able to handle difficult situations; customer service experience preferred. Experience using hardware (laptops, pc’s, printers, scanners, mobile devices), software (Windows, Mac, web browsers, Novasis, Webmail, Brightspace), and wireless network access preferred. Familiarity with the library’s catalog, journals, databases and web search engines preferred. Additional Information: Semester Library Service Hours Monday – Thursday: 8am – 12am Friday: 8am – 5pm Saturday: 9am – 5pm Sunday: 12pm – 12am Building Wildcard Access: 24/7 All student employees must complete hiring paperwork online before they can be hired. Also, new student employees must go to the Human Resources Office in person to show original forms of employment authorization and identification required for the I-9 form. Physical Demands Summary: Prolonged sitting, standing, and walking for up to 4 hours at a time; frequent bending and lifting; able to lift 30 lbs. of library materials while moving/walking; pushing and pulling a book truck (4 wheels) of library materials weighing between 50 and 100 lbs.; ability to climb several flights of stairs on an occasional basis. Wage Rate: $15.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33836": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Professor - Criminology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Professor - Criminology To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include: 1. Cover Letter / Letter of Interest, 2. Resume / Curriculum Vitae, 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy 4. Contact information for three references 5. Official transcripts Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260010F Position Title: Adjunct Professor - Criminology Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 144-Sociology - CRM Position Summary: The Department of Sociology and Criminology at Villanova University seeks qualified individuals for its Criminology Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time. We are particularly seeking faculty to teach multiple sections of Introduction of Criminology. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Visit the Department web page for further information (http://www.villanova.edu/artsci/sociology). For questions, contact Department Chair Allison Ann Payne (allison.payne@villanova.edu). Duties and Responsibilities: Teach courses in Criminology, primarily Introduction to Criminology. Minimum Qualifications: Masters degree in Criminology or a related field. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Criminology or a related field. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include: 1. Cover Letter / Letter of Interest, 2. Resume / Curriculum Vitae, 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy 4. Contact information for three references 5. Official transcripts Posting Date: 02/10/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
