    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36116": {
      "title": "Information Technology Technician II",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Information Technology Technician II - Video Event and Learning Spaces Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Information Technology Technician II - Video Event and Learning Spaces To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must show prior appropriate technological proficiencies. Familiarity with video editing is favorable. Applicants must have references. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260350V Position Title: Information Technology Technician II - Video Event and Learning Spaces Posting Type Student Hours/week: 15 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Widger Law School Building Detailed Work Schedule Day, evening and weekend hours included. Weekday coverage times: 7 am- 9 pm Monday through Friday. Weekend hours also available. Number of positions: 7 Department: 845-UTS - Multimedia Technologies Contact Name: Brian Sirak Contact Phone/Extension: 16105195819 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: This position is open for both graduate and undergrad students. It will focus on video production, supporting staff with editing projects as well as supporting technology in the classrooms across campus. You will also be shooting video, assisting professors in the classroom and assisting staff in other related projects. This job will also require customer service, entering tickets scanning, typing and moderate clerical work. The most integral part of this position is responsibility as you will be working side by side with the professional staff to provide support to faculty and staff throughout the university. You will be trained on how to shoot video with cameras that are used in the professional field and edit video using Final Cut Pro. We do have an excellent training program so a willingness to learn and desire to learn are essential. We do shoots all over campus and cover events almost daily, there is a large editing component to the work and it is a true production shop atmosphere with very quick turnarounds. It is a position that entails a great deal of responsibility but offers great opportunities for both learning and future job placement. Requirements: Must be familiar with Microsoft Teams, Google Docs, and Spreadsheets (Excel, Pages, etc). Must be familiar with Microsoft Office 365, including Teams, Outlook, and Excel Digital editing experience and proficiency – Final Cut Pro or Premiere Proficient in Zoom Must be responsible and be able to provide references. Additional Information: Experience with camera equipment and/or sound equipment helpful Experience with Microsoft Teams Adobe CC Suite experience Cabrini Campus availability helpful Physical Demands Summary: Lifting of camera equipment up to 50 lbs. Walking from Scarpa Hall to all ends of campus for shoots, support, and meetings. Be able to stand for long stretches to record. Wage Rate: $13.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
