    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34018": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Lab Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Lab Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260052V Position Title: Undergraduate Lab Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: >20 hours p/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 2 Department: 202-Civil and Environmental Engineering Contact Name: Dr. Erica Forgione Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-4960 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: An undergraduate student is needed to assist in microplastics analysis under the supervision of Dr. Kelly Good and Dr. Erica Forgione. The student will use a visual microscope to count and categorize particles. Data will be collected and analyzed via Microsoft Excel, R script, Lab Archives, and One Drive. Additional hands-on laboratory soils analysis may also be completed. Requirements: Student must b e able to conduct meticulous, repetitive work that requires high levels of precision. Experience with Microsoft Excel and coding required; R script and previous research experience preferred. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $13.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35247": {
      "title": "Event Chef",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Event Chef - Catering (On Call) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Event Chef - Catering (On Call) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. On call status - schedule will be determined based on needs of the department and various catering functions. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260029T Position Title: Event Chef - Catering (On Call) Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: casual/seasonal Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 423-Catering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. The Event Chef will support and execute catered events per instructions from the Executive Chef on an as needed basis. Acts as lead culinarian for events by supervising the work of the Event Cooks who are on staff during large events. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : This position will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the values of the Villanova Mission and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This position will focus on our Core Values: Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. Prepare and execute menus for catering events, ensuring consistency and high-quality presentation. Collaborate with event planners to accommodate dietary preferences and special requests. Set up and break down cooking stations at event venues, ensuring compliance with food safety and sanitation standards. Manage food inventory, prep work, and ensure timely service during events. Assist with menu planning and suggest creative dishes that align with seasonal ingredients and event themes. Monitor portion control and minimize food waste. Supervise kitchen staff and support team members in a dynamic environment. Maintain a clean, organized, and efficient workspace during events. Adhere to all health and safety regulations while handling food and kitchen equipment. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Assist in day time prep for events Minimum Qualifications: Work Experience: Kitchen experience Work Skills: Strong verbal and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: Culinary degree, preferred Work Experience: Experience in high end and high volume restaurants or catering, preferred Specific Job Knowledge: Proven experience as a chef in catering, banquets, or event-based cooking. Strong knowledge of various cooking techniques, cuisines, and food presentation. Ability to work well under pressure and adapt to different event settings. Excellent time management and organizational skills. Food Handler’s Certification (or willingness to obtain). Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. and stand for extended periods. Flexible schedule, including availability on weekends, evenings, and holidays as needed. Reliable transportation to various event locations. Equipment Knowledge: Knowledge of modern cooking equipment and practices Other: Team player with a willingness to listen to direction and get the job done Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Must have a comprehensive understanding of knife work, time and temperature regulating systems, and ability to work with hot equipment. Environmental conditions: Must be able to work in a loud, hot, noisy environment. Physical requirements: Must be able to work on feet for an extended period of time. Must be able to lift 40 lbs. Special Message to Applicants: On call status – schedule will be determined based on needs of the department and various catering functions. EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 06/04/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Up to $30.00/hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35881": {
      "title": "Dining Services Associate",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Dining Services Associate - Villanova or Radnor, PA Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Dining Services Associate - Villanova or Radnor, PA To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedules available include: Full Time, 12 months (year round): 1.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 2.) Tuesday – Saturday 6am – 3pm 3.) Sunday – Thursday 12pm – 9pm 4.) Sunday – Thursday 4pm – 1am 5.) Tuesday – Saturday 4pm – 1am 6.) Friday – Monday 8am – 7pm 7.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 8.) Friday – Monday 3pm – 2am 9.) Sunday and Monday 12pm – 9pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 5pm – 2am 10.) Sunday – Thursday 12pm – 9pm 11.) Monday/Tuesday/Thursday/Friday/Sunday 12pm - 9pm Full Time, 9 months (these positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 12:30pm – 9:30pm 2.) Monday - Friday 11:30am - 8:30pm Part Time, 9 months (these positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Monday/Wednesday 5pm – 10pm, Saturday/Sunday 9am – 6pm 2.) Friday – Tuesday 6am – 11:30am Please note in your application which shift(s) you are available to work. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260349S Position Title: Dining Services Associate - Villanova or Radnor, PA Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Villanova University’s new Cabrini Campus will open in August 2026! To learn more about the 112-acre campus, including information on the shuttle bus service, please visit the Villanova University, Cabrini Campus page by clicking here. Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. As a Dining Services Associate you will be responsible for maintaining the overall cleanliness, sanitation, and food safety of the dining operations. This includes front of the house and back of the house areas along with receiving and stocking duties. Stocks, rotates, and replenishes merchandise. The Dining Services Associate will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement! The individual will focus on our Core Values: Safety, Sanitation, and Excellence. All of our associates will work hard to improve our systems and overall operation. Why join our team ? Our dining services team members receive: Increased hourly rate starting at $17.50/hour Generous vacation plan and holiday schedule Free meals during each shift Health and wellness resources plus discount programs Opportunities for advancement Various schedules available, including late night positions with night differential Free uniforms, including footwear *Full-time employees also receive: 403b retirement plan with employer base and matching contributions, tuition remission for associates and dependents, medical, vision, and dental insurance with multiple health plan options Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Scrapes, cleans, sanitizes, and replenishes all dishes, silverware, cups, glasses, pots, and pans etc. Properly stores all clean items. Operates dish machine or pot machine and is responsible to record proper temperatures and correct levels of chemical sanitizers according to regulations. Loads and unloads dish machine. Disposes of food waste and trash both front of house and back of house as needed. Sweeps and mops all floors and walk in refrigerators. Separates recycling from trash. Assists in receiving, storing, transporting and stocking of food and nonfood items. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Assists in transporting supplies from storage areas to work areas as required. Fills juices, milk, and soda machines as needed. Assists on serving lines or back of the house prep work if needed. Acts as a runner to replenish food supplies on service lines. Communicates with cooks concerning amounts of food on service lines. Works special events/weekends as required Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Work Skills: Basic reading and writing skills; basic communication skills. Excellent customer service skills. Practices excellent personal hygiene habits and follows and adheres to uniform standards. Ability to: follow directions and complete assigned tasks, work with minimal supervision, and to interact with people on a constant basis. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred – High school diploma or equivalent Preferred – Basic knowledge of food service safety and sanitation Preferred – Serv Safe Training and Allergy Awareness Training Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Knives, slicers, and all kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: Chemicals used for cleaning Weather exposure for special events Physical Requirements: Ability to stand for extended periods Ability to lift, push/pull up to 50 pounds independently Ability to withstand extreme temperatures Special Message to Applicants: Schedules available include: Full Time, 12 months (year round): 1.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 2.) Tuesday – Saturday 6am – 3pm 3.) Sunday – Thursday 12pm – 9pm 4.) Sunday – Thursday 4pm – 1am 5.) Tuesday – Saturday 4pm – 1am 6.) Friday – Monday 8am – 7pm 7.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 8.) Friday – Monday 3pm – 2am 9.) Sunday and Monday 12pm – 9pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 5pm – 2am 10.) Sunday – Thursday 12pm – 9pm 11.) Monday/Tuesday/Thursday/Friday/Sunday 12pm – 9pm Full Time, 9 months (these positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 12:30pm – 9:30pm 2.) Monday – Friday 11:30am – 8:30pm Part Time, 9 months (these positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Monday/Wednesday 5pm – 10pm, Saturday/Sunday 9am – 6pm 2.) Friday – Tuesday 6am – 11:30am Please note in your application which shift(s) you are available to work. Posting Date: 07/14/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $17.50 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 0 Maximum Number of References Needed 0 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Please select the location you are interested in working at (select all that apply) Cabrini Campus (Radnor PA) Villanova Campus (Villanova PA) * Please select the shift(s) you are available to work. Please select all that apply. Friday - Monday 2pm - 1am Tuesday-Saturday 6am-3pm Sunday-Thursday 12pm - 9pm Sunday -Thursday 4pm-1am Tuesday-Saturday 4pm - 1am Friday-Monday 8am-7pm Friday - Monday 2pm -1am Friday-Monday 3pm - 2am Sunday and Monday 12pm-9pm. Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday 5pm - 2am Sunday - Thursday 12pm - 9pm Sunday - Thursday 12:30pm - 9:30pm Monday and Wednesday 5pm - 10pm, Saturday and Sunday 9am - 6pm Friday - Tuesday 6am - 11:30am Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
