    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33428": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Accounting",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty, Accounting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty, Accounting To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Accounting and Information Systems Department will accept applications until position is filled. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2012021F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty, Accounting Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 217-Accountancy Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Accounting for undergraduate and MBA courses. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester. The applicant must be committed to excellence in the teaching of accounting. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching specific Accounting courses. Minimum Qualifications: The applicant must be committed to excellence in business education. A master’s degree within a relevant field is strongly preferred. Equivalent experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: PhD or terminal degree in a related field or similar professional experience in a related field. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Accounting and Information Systems Department will accept applications until position is filled. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 11/19/2013 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,925.00 – $2,505.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed Maximum Number of References Needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
