      "title": "Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Teaching Assistant - Sustainable Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Teaching Assistant - Sustainable Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260261V Position Title: Teaching Assistant - Sustainable Engineering Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 5 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 207-Sustainable Engineering Program Contact Name: Natalie MacNamara Contact Phone/Extension: 6105197253 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Sustainable Engineering Program is seeking a motivated graduate level student to serve as teaching assistant for the Fundamentals – Sustainable Engineering course ( SUSE 7110) in the Fall 2026 semester and for Advanced LCA & Intro to Product Design ( SUSE 8111) in the Spring 2027 semester. Requirements: Responsibilities include but are not limited to: • Grade assignments and/or exams as needed • Provide guidance to students as needed • Assist faculty instructor as needed • Provide feedback on student performance Additional Information: Student(s) will be working with Dr. Mary McRae, Assistant Teaching Professor, Sustainable Engineering. Minimal qualifications: • Graduate level student • Detail oriented • Must be able to work independently • Software skills of Excel, SimaPro and certain climate modeling sites • Ability to use Brightspace • Ability to maintain confidentiality while working with sensitive information Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $18.00/hour Graduate-level Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
