    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36039": {
      "title": "Director of Athletics Compliance",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Director of Athletics Compliance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Director of Athletics Compliance To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260402S Position Title: Director of Athletics Compliance Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 772-Athl - Compliance Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Support the Senior Associate Athletics Director, in the day-to-day oversight of the Athletics Compliance Office. The director will assist in all aspects of administering the NCAA Compliance program for a Division I Athletics Department with 24 varsity programs and will be the primary liaison for assigned sports. Must perform all duties within University, Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in the oversight of compliance operations for assigned sports. Process all NCAA waivers and violations Work with Director of Compliance/Financial Aid to issue National Letter of Intent and Grant-in-Aid scholarship letters. Conduct initial eligibility evaluations on all recruited prospective student-athletes to ensure adherence to NCAA standards. Oversee all aspects of recruiting. Monitor and approve official and unofficial visits. Oversee approval process for camps and clinics. Coordinate the usage of recruiting software ( ARMS ). Produce, send and ensure receipt of notification of transfer requests. Monitor and approve prospective student-athlete ticket requests. Prepare, organize, and administer a comprehensive NCAA rules education program for athletics staff, student-athletes, boosters/alumni and staff outside of athletics. Provide NCAA and Big East rules interpretations for coaches, student-athletes, athletic department staff, constituency groups, boosters, and the Villanova community. Review and approve all activities involving student-athletes and promotional activities, employment, and other requests. Review and monitor Athletic Development, Athletic Communication and Marketing activities to ensure consistent compliance. Assist in Name, Image, Likeness activities, including rules education and monitoring and collaborate with third party in post-House execution. Serve as the Athletics Compliance Office lead for all sports in the areas of NCAA Bylaws 16 (Awards, Benefits, and Expenses) & 17 (Playing & Practice Seasons). Oversee the onboarding process for coaches and staff. Lead for Teamworks/C&R/Influencer education for athletics department staff. Serve as the Athletics Compliance Office liaison to assigned campus units. Perform other duties, as assigned by VP/Director of Athletics or Associate AD for Compliance. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelors Degree required. Minimum Work Experience 3+ years of experience in sports administration, specifically in compliance. Work Skills Must possess excellent organizational skills and the ability to perform accurate, detailed work under time pressures. Strong interpersonal communication skills combined with the ability to interact with diverse groups. Specific Job Knowledge Working knowledge of the collegiate basketball landscape as it relates to NCAA /Conference/Institutional bylaws and regulations. Job Specific Knowledge Proficiency with personal computer applications and comfortable with various computer programs (Microsoft Office, Excel, LSDBi, ARMS , Teamworks). Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: Master’s Degree in Sport Administration or related field or Law Degree preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Flexibility to travel occasionally and work nights and weekends. Professional work environment. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/17/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 14 and the range is $58,300-72,900. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 14 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 5 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tBasketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches?        Y         N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tCurrent VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes?    Y     N Yes No * How many years of experience in sports administration, specifically in compliance, do you have? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
