    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34040": {
      "title": "The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include: cover letter resume/curriculum vitae statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) and a statement on inclusive excellence are required at time of interview. Contact information for 3 individual references are required for all finalists. Required for appointment: • Official transcripts from undergraduate and graduate degrees. • Evidence of professional liability insurance. • Criminal background check clearance. • FBI fingerprints and PA Child Abuse Clearances. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260018F Position Title: The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 232-Nursing Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The M. Louise Fitzpatrick College of Nursing at Villanova University invites applications for the inaugural Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Family Endowed Professorships in Oncology Nursing, a distinguished tenured faculty appointment for a teacher-scholar dedicated to advancing excellence in cancer care through nursing scholarship, education, clinical practice, and leadership. We seek a visionary oncology nursing scholar, educator, and leader with a strong national and/or international reputation who will elevate the College’s impact in cancer research, interprofessional education, and clinical innovation. Supported by dedicated funding, the Endowed Professor will drive transformative research, cultivate interdisciplinary partnerships within the Philadelphia region’s renowned cancer ecosystem, mentor and educate the next generation of nurse leaders, and shape conversations that advance cancer care nationally and globally. The Endowed Professor will teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels within the Fitzpatrick College of Nursing. We also anticipate an affiliation with Fox Chase Cancer Center , an NCI -designated Comprehensive Cancer Center and ANCC -recognized Magnet® hospital based in Philadelphia, PA. Options related to this potential partnership will be discussed with candidates as part of the interview process. The opportunity for collaboration provides a robust clinical and research home to support sustained scholarly and practice excellence. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Lead a nationally and/or internationally recognized program of oncology nursing research. Secure external funding to support innovative research and programmatic initiatives. Publish in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals and present at leading academic and clinical conferences. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in oncology nursing and related areas. Mentor faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and undergraduate and graduate students in research and professional development. Build and sustain regional and national collaborations that influence oncology practice, policy, and education. Design and launch a forward-looking Oncology Nursing certificate or graduate focus within the Fitzpatrick College of Nursing. Facilitate the development of an Oncology Nursing Consortium with peer Schools of Nursing. Serve in leadership roles within the College, University, and professional organizations. Demonstrate a strong commitment to inclusive excellence in research, teaching, and clincal practice. Establish a robust research program and/or clinical practice through a potential joint appointment at Fox Chase Cancer Center. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: PhD or equivalent terminal degree in Nursing or a related field. Specific Job Knowledge and Skills: Eligibility for RN licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Established national reputation in oncology nursing, evidenced by sustained scholarly productivity, external funding, and professional leadership. A distinguished record of achievement that qualifies the candidate for an appointment at the rank of Professor. Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentorship. Experience mentoring DNP and PhD students. Strong alignment with the mission and values of the Fitzpatrick College of Nursing, including commitments to holistic health, social justice, and service. Embrace Villanova University’s teacher–scholar model. Preferred Qualifications: Oncology nursing certification (e.g., OCN®, AOCN®, or equivalent). Experience in interdisciplinary, translational, or community-engaged research. Proven record of impactful partnerships with clinical institutions or cancer centers. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include: cover letter resume/curriculum vitae statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) and a statement on inclusive excellence are required at time of interview. Contact information for 3 individual references are required for all finalists. Required for appointment: • Official transcripts from undergraduate and graduate degrees. • Evidence of professional liability insurance. • Criminal background check clearance. • FBI fingerprints and PA Child Abuse Clearances. Posting Date: 03/09/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35294": {
      "title": "Student Peer Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Peer Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Peer Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260227V Position Title: Student Peer Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work Study ONLY Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Kintsuba Hall Detailed Work Schedule Must have FEDERAL WORK - STUDY eligibility (not just student employment) Work Hours: Number of positions: 1 Department: 295-Office of Financial Assistance Contact Name: Marykay Klara Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7933 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Provide support in key areas of customer service and clerical assistance for the office. Duties include: answering phones & returning calls to students and parents, retrieving phone messages from voice mail, greeting visitors to the office and answering general financial aid questions for students and parents. Requirements: Only eligible FEDERAL Work-Study students may apply. Wear appropriate attire for office setting. Arrive on/time for shift schedule and obtain a replacement from other office Peers if unable to work a shift. Additional Information: Hours Available: Shifts are available any time from 8:30 a.m. until 4:30 p.m. Able to work during fall, winter and spring breaks preferred but not required. Available to work for Admitted Prospective Student Candidate Day. Discreet confidentiality a must. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 05/14/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
