    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36171": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant - SETR Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant - SETR Lab To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260365V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant - SETR Lab Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 10 hours p/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Structural Eng. Teaching and Research Lab Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1-5 Department: 202-Civil and Environmental Engineering Contact Name: Linda DeAngelis Contact Phone/Extension: 9-4960 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Students filling the position will assist in the preparation of undergraduate laboratories and graduate research projects related to steel, concrete, wood, masonry, and composite materials in the SETRL (Structural Engineering Teaching & Research Laboratory). Students will be expected to work independently and together with graduate students, faculty and staff. In addition to assisting with the preparation of laboratory experiments, students will also be expected to aid in the organization and collection of data, general lab maintenance, and cleanup activities. Students should expect to gain hands on knowledge of structural engineering materials and construction practices, which will enhance their undergraduate experience and further prepare them for graduate school or future employment. Requirements: Student must be enrolled in the Department of Civil & Environmental Engineering with an interest in structural engineering. Some proficiency in AutoCAD and Microsoft Office is expected. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: After the proper training is complete, students will be expected to operate the following tools and equipment: horizontal band saw, milling machine, drill press, annular cutter, circular saw, compound miter saw, concrete/brick saw, angle grinder, concrete vibrator, concrete mixer, and others. Operation of the SETRL overhead crane may also be part of the daily tasks, after appropriate OSHA training conducted by VU Environmental Health and Safety. Wage Rate: $15/hr. Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33430": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - School of Law Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - School of Law To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants must apply online and include: a letter of interest (including the names and email address for at least 3 references), current curriculum vitae, a statement describing your teaching philosophy, including courses you are interested in teaching, academic transcripts; unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2021849F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - School of Law Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 241-Law School Instruction Position Summary: Charles Widger School of Law seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time. The School of Law offers programs leading to a JD degree. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching law school courses. Duties will vary with the specific courses being taught. Minimum Qualifications: JD degree; must be committed to excellence in law school education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All applicants must apply online and include: a letter of interest (including the names and email address for at least 3 references), current curriculum vitae, a statement describing your teaching philosophy, including courses you are interested in teaching, academic transcripts; unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Posting Date: 09/17/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position has a salary of $1,500.00 per credit hour. This may be pro-rated in the case of team-teaching scenarios where effort is shared. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * What is your area of expertise (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    80