    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34235": {
      "title": "Recreation Center Supervisor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Recreation Center Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Recreation Center Supervisor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260066V Position Title: Recreation Center Supervisor Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 20 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Cabrini Detailed Work Schedule This position has primarily nights and weekend hours. Number of positions: Until all are filled Department: 775-Athl - Intramurals Contact Name: Michael Hay Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-6573 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Recreation Center Supervisors will work under the direction of the Recreation Center Operations Coordinator and Aquatics Coordinator to manage a staff of student Recreation Center Attendants and Lifeguards as they carry out overall day-to-day operations in The Dixon Center and surrounding outdoor recreational facilities. Recreation Center Supervisors will assist in the ongoing supervision, training, and evaluation of Recreation Center Attendants and Lifeguards. Supervisors will also serve as the on-site operations manager during early morning, evening, and weekend shifts, when professional staff members may be off-site. Requirements: Supervise recreational facilities and enforce recreation center policies and procedures, ensuring a safe environment for recreational activities. Oversee Recreation Center operations and provide direct supervision, guidance, operational support and training to Recreation Center Attendants and Lifeguards. Stay current on fitness and recreation programs and operational procedures to provide exceptional customer service to Villanova community members. Create a welcoming and positive experience for users. Assist in the ongoing evaluation of student Recreation Center Attendants and Lifeguards. Uphold Recreation Center Attendant and Lifeguard job expectations, ensuring appropriate staffing and operational support throughout the Dixon Center and surrounding recreational facilities. Assist Recreation Center Attendant with their responsibilities when necessary and appropriate. Provide regular feedback and ongoing input to professional staff members for the purpose of refining policies, improving operational procedures, and enhancing services offered. Attend ongoing Recreation Center Supervisor training sessions. Attend and assist in the development and implementation of ongoing student employee training sessions for Recreation Center Attendants and Lifeguards. Enact or assist in emergency response. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: May be asked to carry/move fitness and recreation equipment. Must be able to lift 45 lbs. May be asked to perform duties at outdoor recreational facilities, in various seasons with the possibility of inclement weather. Wage Rate: $15/hr Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Other Document Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Resume / Curriculum Vitae Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
