    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35632": {
      "title": "Clay Center/O’Donnell Center Student Events Team",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Clay Center/O’Donnell Center Student Events Team Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Clay Center/O’Donnell Center Student Events Team To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260264V Position Title: Clay Center/O’Donnell Center Student Events Team Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-12 hours Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Bartley Hall Detailed Work Schedule Available days, nights and infrequent weekend events that are scheduled throughout the academic year. Must work at least every two weeks. Number of positions: 20-25 Department: 257-Clay Center Contact Name: Kathy Mongiello Contact Phone/Extension: 9-4333 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Join the Clay Center/O’Donnell Center events team of students assistants and experience the behind the scenes of our events. Applicants must convey a professional demeanor for this position as there will be interaction with campus and corporate partners. Responsibilities include, but not limited to, setting up and breaking down event space, checking in guests, and other event related tasks. Event assistants will be required to be on premises before, during and after events they sign up to work. Requirements: Good interpersonal skills required, flexible availability for days, evenings, and very infrequent weekend event. Commit to working at least every 2 weeks. This job commitment requires at least a 4 hour set up shift per week in Bartley Hall Monday through Thursday from 4:30 to 8:30 pm for events. Day and weekend events times will vary depending on the program. You are expected to work the shift you selected for the entire semester. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Able to move and lift objects up to 30 lbs. Wage Rate: $10.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 05/03/2027 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
