    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35807": {
      "title": "Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Operations Assistant - External Relations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Operations Assistant - External Relations To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260275V Position Title: Operations Assistant - External Relations Posting Type Student Hours/week: 8-10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Bartley Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 222-Marketing Contact Name: Yvonne Poorman-Taylor Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-4350 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Marketing & Business Law Department’s External Relations & Operations Assistant will support the faculty and the Department Administrator in planning and executing events, external relations, and data management. The position provides the opportunity to have a direct impact on the perception of the Marketing & Business Law department within the Villanova School of Business and among its alumni through the creation and execution of events, communication with alumni, friends, and donors, and additional support. The individual will interact with alumni, donors, faculty, and staff. Other tasks may include conducting research on VSB alumni, outreach, and assembling mailings. Requirements: Knowledge of the Marketing major and Business Law minor. A demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office tools. Advanced organizational and time management skills. Superior attention to deal. Ability to exercise discretion, confidentiality, and good judgment to compile research using common tools such as LinkedIn and Google. Excellent written and oral communication skills. The ability to prioritize and multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Must be a problem-solver, self-starter, and capable of finding solutions with minimal oversight. An ability to work with and communicate appropriately with alumni, guests, and faculty/staff leadership. Design skills (Canva, Photoshop, etc.) a plus. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: This job requires lifting or carrying general equipment or supplies (up to 30 pounds) to and from events. Wage Rate: $11.25 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
