    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35314": {
      "title": "Lab Assistant- Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Lab Assistant- Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Lab Assistant- Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260221V Position Title: Lab Assistant- Engineering Posting Type Student Hours/week: 15-20 hrs/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Typically 15-20 hours/week is anticipated. Number of positions: 2 Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Contact Name: Mackenzie Bonney Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-8762 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Join our team as an Engineering Lab Assistant at the Drosdick Innovation Lab in the Villanova College of Engineering! As a Lab Assistant, you’ll play a crucial role in supporting the operations of our new state-of-the-art makerspace, where students, faculty, and staff come together to explore, create, and innovate. You’ll have the opportunity to work with cutting-edge equipment, assist with workshops and events, and help foster a dynamic and inclusive maker community. If you’re passionate about engineering, hands-on learning, and making a difference, this is the perfect role for you! Requirements: Requirements: Currently enrolled as a student in the Villanova College of Engineering. Experience with at least one of the following areas: electronics, 3D printing, computer-aided design ( CAD ), or woodworking. Ability to commit to working 10-15 hours per week, but up to 20 hours if desired. Strong problem-solving skills and mechanical aptitude, with a willingness to learn new skills and techniques. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively in a team environment. Detail-oriented with a focus on quality and safety in all aspects of work. Reliable, responsible, and punctual, with a positive attitude and a passion for making and innovation. Responsibilities: Perform regular maintenance and repairs on equipment, including 3D printers, laser cutters, CNC machines, and other tools. Assist and participate in workshops, events, and training sessions held in the lab. Help students and faculty with their projects by providing technical support, guidance, and troubleshooting assistance. Clean and organize the lab space to ensure a safe and efficient working environment. Collaborate with lab staff and faculty to develop new procedures, protocols, and resources for lab users. Maintain inventory of supplies and materials Uphold lab policies and procedures, and ensure compliance with safety regulations and guidelines. Other duties as assigned to support the operations and mission of the Drosdick Innovation Lab. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: The Innovation Lab is two floors accessible by stairs, however, accessibility accommodations can be made if necessary. Wage Rate: $13/hr Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your major, minor and GPA? (Open Ended Question) * What is your class year? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior None of the above * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Please explain what interests you about this position. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience operating 3D printers, laser cutters, CNC machines, or other tools commonly found in a makerspace? If so, please describe your level of proficiency and any specific projects you've worked on using these tools. (Open Ended Question) * Are you familiar with computer-aided design (CAD) software such as SolidWorks, OnShape, AutoCAD, or Fusion 360? Please provide details about your experience with these programs and any projects you've completed using them. (Open Ended Question) * Please provide details of any other applicable skills or experiences that you believe will contribute to your effectiveness in this position. (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35908": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins immediately and continues until position is filled. All initial applications are to include: • Application letter • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial Graduate Transcripts • Sample of working papers • Names of three references • Finalists will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. Please ensure that materials evidence qualifications and address duties and responsibilities. Other information will be required if the candidate makes it into the interview round. For technical assistance, please contact us at 610-519-7900, 610-519-7616, or jobshelp@villanova.edu. Application related questions may be sent to Dr. Denise Hanes Downey, Associate Chair and KPMG Endowed Professor in Accounting (denise.downey@villanova.edu). Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260060F Position Title: Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 217-Accountancy Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Accounting and Information Systems in the Villanova School of Business is seeking applications for a Tenure Track position beginning Fall 2027. This person will report to the Chair of the Accounting and Information Systems Department. Our primary recruiting focus is at the rank of Assistant Professor; both recent graduates and experienced Assistant Professors are encouraged to apply. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: This person will primarily teach courses at the undergraduate level, and is expected to incorporate AI and other discipline-related emerging technologies into related coursework. The faculty member is expected to publish high quality research in any area of accounting, targeting top peer-reviewed academic journals. Service expectations are commensurate with hiring level and candidate’s prior experience, and will include participating in curriculum development activities and engagement with students, alumni and the broader accounting community. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. with some relevant teaching experience, potential to publish in high quality journals, and a willingness to work in a collegial environment. Preferred Qualifications: A Ph.D. with a demonstrated track record of high-quality teaching across courses in the financial and managerial accounting series as well as evidence of excellence in working with students. An ability to innovate within the curriculum. Professional experience with a CPA license is also preferred. Demonstrated willingness to work with other faculty and contribute to a collegial environment. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins immediately and continues until position is filled. All initial applications are to include: • Application letter • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial Graduate Transcripts • Sample of working papers • Names of three references • Finalists will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. Please ensure that materials evidence qualifications and address duties and responsibilities. Other information will be required if the candidate makes it into the interview round. For technical assistance, please contact us at 610-519-7900, 610-519-7616, or jobshelp@villanova.edu. Application related questions may be sent to Dr. Denise Hanes Downey, Associate Chair and KPMG Endowed Professor in Accounting (denise.downey@villanova.edu). Posting Date: 08/03/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample/Publications Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
