    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35550": {
      "title": "Media Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Media Assistant - Undergraduate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Media Assistant - Undergraduate To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260254V Position Title: Media Assistant - Undergraduate Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-15 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule | Position begins in the Fall 2026 Semester, 8/24/26 Number of positions: 2 Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Contact Name: Therese Wosczyna Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-3948 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The College of Engineering is seeking two creative and motivated student leaders to collaborate with COE’s Communication & Marketing and Engineering Recruitment teams to develop engaging, year-round social media content. These students will play a key role in showcasing the Villanova Engineering experience through authentic storytelling, event coverage, and student-driven campaigns. Key Responsibilities Create social media content highlighting College of Engineering events, programs, and student experiences. Capture and produce short-form video content (e.g., Instagram Reels, TikTok-style videos, stories). Conduct and feature student interviews, day-in-the-life content, and event coverage. Lead and participate in social media takeovers to provide authentic student perspectives. Identify and develop student-centered content based on social media trends. Work closely with the Communications team to ensure branding consistency and strategic messaging. Attend select campus events and outreach programs to gather content. Qualifications Current Villanova University student. Strong interest in social media, marketing, storytelling, or communications. Experience with content creation tools (e.g., Instagram, TikTok, Canva, Adobe Suite) preferred. Excellent communication and organizational skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating with a team. Creative mindset with attention to detail and brand alignment. Time Commitment Approximately 10 hours per week (flexible based on schedule and event calendar). Benefits Gain hands-on experience in marketing, communications, and digital storytelling. Build a professional portfolio of social media and video content. Work closely with Communications and Engineering leadership. Play a key role in shaping the narrative of the Villanova Engineering student experience. Application must include: Cover letter CV/Resume Three samples of previous related work or what your vision of social media content would look like. Requirements: Undergraduate students at the sophomore level or above Additional Information: Student(s) will be working with Heather Gill Physical Demands Summary: Normal activities (possible lifting of ~20 lbs.) Wage Rate: $13.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
