    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33452": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2018489F Position Title: Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Summary: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Villanova University is seeking applications for adjunct faculty positions. The department offers a wide variety of courses in analog and digital electronics, computer architecture, cybersecurity, microwaves, energy systems and signals and communications. Further information about the department can be found at http://www1.villanova.edu/villanova/engineering/departments/ece.html. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: The minimum qualification is a Master’s degree in electrical or computer engineering or a related field. Commitment to teaching excellence is expected. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Undergraduate courses are offered during the day; most graduate courses run during the evening. Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 05/11/2018 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34996": {
      "title": "Receiving Clerk",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Receiving Clerk - (Cascia Student Center Cabrini Campus) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Receiving Clerk - (Cascia Student Center Cabrini Campus) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours Monday - Friday 6am - 3pm Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260121S Position Title: Receiving Clerk - (Cascia Student Center Cabrini Campus) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Receiving Clerk is responsible for receiving and maintaining records of all food products, supplies, and merchandise and keeping accurate record of inventory on hand, used, and ordered. This individual in this position will also serve as the delivery driver as needed for on campus deliveries. The Receiving Clerk will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Cleanliness and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Inspect, receive, and record all food and supplies delivered according to safe food handling guidelines and procedures. Responsible for returning and refusing items. Date and store all food and supplies according to safe food handling guidelines and procedures utilizing the FIFO system of inventory. Maintain accurate inventory records of all food products, supplies, and merchandise entered into the building. Maintain order and cleanliness of all food and non-food storage areas. Drives University vehicles for Dining Services as needed. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High school degree or equivalent. Minimum Work Experience: 1+ year as a receiver or related experience in dealing with inventory control. Work Skills: Must possess math skills to keep records of inventory on hand, used, and ordered. Must possess a valid driver’s license and must be an approved University driver in accordance with the University’s motor vehicle record policy for drivers. Must be able to follow directions and complete assigned tasks. Must have basic and effective communication skills and basic reading and writing skills. Must be able to work with minimal supervision and follow directions and complete assigned tasks. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, Machinery, and Equipment Used: Kitchen Equipment. Environmental Conditions: Ability to use chemicals daily, and use proper protective equipment as called for by the specific chemical and task. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift, push, pull up to 50 lbs independently. Ability to withstand extreme temperatures (hot/cold). Ability to use chemicals. Special Message to Applicants: The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours Monday – Friday 6am – 3pm Posting Date: 04/09/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98/hr. shift differential added for qualifying shifts Salary Grade: 10 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35819": {
      "title": "Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Night (3rd) Shift: 10pm - 6:30am; Sunday-Thursday Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260368S Position Title: Custodian (Night Shift/3rd Shift) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 809-Custodial Services Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Under the moderate direction of a supervisor, performs general cleaning duties within dormitory, office, and other public facilities areas. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: TYPICAL JOB DUTIES Pick up and dispose of trash, to include the proper handling of recyclable materials. Dusts, sweeps, and/or dry mops. Wet mops and/or spot mops. Operates walk-behind or ride-on floor machine, wet vac, & carpet extractor. • Cleans glass: • All inside areas that can be safely reached. All entrance glass, including doors, inside and out. Sanitizes washrooms, showers, and toilet facilities (dormitories only). Fills all dispensers in restrooms. Vacuums and cleans carpets and walk-off mats. • Washes walls, woodwork, light fixtures, inside of windows, and other glass. Removes snow and ice and cleans and/or picks up debris, such as leaves and paper, around entrances and fire exits (including fire escapes [dormitories only]) from the steps, and from the steps and walkways (generally distanced of ten feet or less) leading to buildings. Reports to immediate supervisor or to work control damage and/or malfunction of equipment observed within assigned areas. Performs other duties assigned within the normal scope of the department’s responsibilities and the individual’s capabilities. Minimum Qualifications: H.S. Diploma or equivalent Ability to follow both written and oral directions. Ability to interact with customers(students, faculty, administration), co-workers and supervisors in a positive and helpful manner. Must be able to climb ladders, to bend and reach, and to lift(up to 60 lbs.) Preferred Qualifications: H.S. Diploma or equivalent. 1 to 3 years of experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Must be able to climb ladders, bend and reach, and lift up to 60 lbs. Special Message to Applicants: Night (3rd) Shift: 10pm – 6:30am; Sunday-Thursday Posting Date: 07/23/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $19.97+$1.75 shift differential = $21.72 an hour Salary Grade: UNION Job Classification: union References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
