    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31109": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science will start reviewing applications on March 1, 2023, but will keep accepting applications until the position is filled. All applicants must apply online and complete a faculty profile. Applications must include: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. A research statement. A teaching statement. A statement of commitment to the principles of diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI). Two letters of recommendation, the system will request the letters directly from the references when appropriate in the process. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20231007F Position Title: Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 182-Astronomy and Planetary Science Position Summary: Villanova University’s Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science invites applications for the Mendel postdoctoral research fellowship. The Mendel fellowship is a flagship postdoctoral opportunity for the candidates seeking to stay in academia. The fellowship provides training and development in all three areas of academic life: research, teaching and service. A successful applicant will join Andrej Prsa’s research team and work on cutting-edge theoretical and observational aspects of binary and multiple stellar populations. In parallel, the applicant will teach an undergraduate core science course/lab to non- STEM majors, where the stress is on incorporating four critical components in a meaningful way: problem solving, laboratory experience, technology and quantitative tools, and interdisciplinary understanding. Finally, the applicant will join the Departmental ecosphere and participate in shaping the future of research and education at Villanova. The Mendel postdoctoral fellowship is a 2-year appointment, with the possibility of extending it for another year. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: A successful applicant will be expected to: Demonstrate the highest regard for the diverse, equitable and inclusive Departmental culture and uphold the true and complete respect for all students, staff and faculty. Partake in state-of-the-art research in theoretical and observational stellar astrophysics, computation astrophysics, astrostatistics, and/or exoplanetary science. Teach 2 sections of the Mendel core science courses or labs per semester (currently “How old is the Universe?”, “Life in the Universe”, “Planetary skies and landscapes”, “Birth and Death of Stars”, “Earth – our habitable world”, and “Earth – a cosmic connection”). Participate in Departmental affairs: meetings, colloquia, events and functions. This includes working with and counseling undergraduate students, contributing to public events and advancing the Department’s reputation and renown locally, nationally and internationally. Minimum Qualifications: A PhD in Physics, Astrophysics, Data Science or a closely related discipline is required. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching : prior experience in teaching STEM classes to non- STEM majors is desired. Research : strong background in physics, astrophysics, statistics and programming is desired. Service : track record of the ability to work with others and to demonstrate diversity awareness is desired. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science will start reviewing applications on March 1, 2023, but will keep accepting applications until the position is filled. All applicants must apply online and complete a faculty profile. Applications must include: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. A research statement. A teaching statement. A statement of commitment to the principles of diversity, equity and inclusion ( DEI ). Two letters of recommendation, the system will request the letters directly from the references when appropriate in the process. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 02/21/2023 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 05/01/2023 Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) What science field is your PhD in? Physics Astrophysics Computer/Data science Mathematics/Statistics Closely related field If your answer above was a \"Closely related field,\" please provide it here. (Open Ended Question) What programming experience and computing infrastructure background do you have? Select all that apply. C/C++/C# Python Java/Javascript HTML and web deployment IDL Bash scripting HPC/MPI environments Virtual reality visualization (vizard, unity, ...) Linux operating system Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Interests Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Contribution to DEI Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36183": {
      "title": "Faculty Services Administrator",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Faculty Services Administrator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Faculty Services Administrator To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260416S Position Title: Faculty Services Administrator Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 100-Provost Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Faculty Services Administrator provides outstanding service to faculty and academic department partners as well as operational support to the Faculty Services Team within the Office of the Provost. Under the direction of the Director, Faculty Services, this position supports the Faculty Services Team with recruitment, onboarding, records management, payroll preparation, faculty relocation administration and orientation stipends for new faculty. The Administrator serves as a key point of contact for routine inquiries, data management tasks, and process coordination for full time, and adjunct faculty. The Administrator contributes to a high-quality service environment by demonstrating responsiveness, accuracy, customer service, discretion, and collaborative problem solving. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Faculty Recruitment, Onboarding, and Records Support Provide support to the Assistant Directors with coordination of recruitment and hiring processes for full time, and adjunct faculty, including scheduling, communication, and tracking documentation. Prepare and route onboarding materials, offer letter templates, and required forms to new faculty members; ensure timely collection of personal information and compliance related documentation. Maintain electronic and physical faculty files; update faculty data in the Enterprise Resource Planning system ( ERP ) and related systems under direction of the Assistant Directors. Monitor and track compliance requirements (clearances, new hire documentation, and trainings). Support routine data entry and updates related to faculty employment changes (hires, reappointments, separations, leaves) ensuring data integrity Serve as a resource to departments with standard questions regarding procedures, paperwork, and timelines. Data Reporting, Documentation, and HRIS Support Serve as a data steward to ensure accuracy and reliability of Office of the Provost data within systems of record and reporting Support the Assistant Director Full-time Faculty Services with the tracking of sabbaticals, retirements and leaves and sending notifications as necessary. Support the Assistant Director Part time Faculty Services with the inactivating adjunct faculty not currently teaching and terminating those who have not taught in three years. Assist in maintaining files for H-1B and J-1 faculty, ensuring documents are filed and updated accurately in close coordination with the Office for Internal Students and Scholars. Develop and generate reporting and compile data under the direction of the Assistant Directors to support academic reporting, analysis, and compliance needs. Update tracking spreadsheets, documentation, and internal procedures. Assist in ensuring data integrity through routine cross‑checks and auditing tasks. Payroll Processing Support Support adjunct payroll process including reconciling monthly payroll, supplemental pay and tenure waiver forms. Support preparation of payroll materials for full-time faculty summer support payments and orientation stipends Assist with producing annual salary notification letters and maintaining accurate payroll records. Assist in collecting, verifying, and preparing data for payroll entry; collaborate with Payroll Services to address basic questions or corrections. Faculty Relocation Administration Support Provide concierge service to new faculty and assist with processing relocation documentation, purchase orders, invoices, and reimbursements; coordinate with Procurement as needed. Provide initial guidance to new faculty on relocation-related steps and requirements. Track the status of moving arrangements and ensure timely submission of forms. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education High School Diploma required. Work Experience Minimum 3 years of experience in an administrative, HR, payroll, or operations role required. Strong organizational skills with high attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks, prioritize effectively, and meet deadlines. Demonstrated professionalism, discretion, and ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Strong customer service orientation and ability to work collaboratively across departments. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and comfort with databases and electronic workflow systems. Willingness to learn complex academic and HR processes as part of a professional growth pathway. Basic understanding of HR processes, employment documentation, and record‑keeping requirements. Familiarity with HRIS , applicant tracking systems, or student information systems preferred. Proficiency with standard office equipment, computers, printers, scanners, and digital records tools. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree with coursework or a degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field preferred. Experience in higher education, academic affairs, or faculty support strongly preferred. Experience with onboarding or employment processes is beneficial. Knowledge of higher education structures and academic personnel processes is preferred. Experience with Banner, PeopleAdmin, Workday or similar ERP and onboarding systems preferred Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Frequent computer work and extended periods of sitting. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/27/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 14 and the range is $58,300-72,900. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 14 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least  3 years of experience in an administrative, HR, payroll, or operations role? Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33435": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - College of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - College of Nursing To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The College of Nursing will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20241126F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - College of Nursing Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 232-Nursing Position Summary: Villanova University College of Nursing has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct (part-time) faculty to provide instruction in the classroom in a variety of courses. Further information about the College of Nursing can be found at www.villanova.edu/nursing. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Understand the course objectives for the course which adjunct faculty is assigned and be familiar with the overall curriculum of the College of Nursing. Provide supervision of students in the classroom (in-person or online) setting. Assist the students to accomplish objectives of the course. Validate students’ understanding of theoretical, scientific and evidence based concepts to meet course objectives. Evaluate and provide feedback to students on their accomplishment of course objectives. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in discipline; licensure or eligibility for licensure in speciality, if applicable (such as nutrition, nursing, etc.) in Pennsylvania. Experience in discipline required. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in academic teaching and willingness to be flexible in fulfilling responsibilities. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The College of Nursing will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Date: 05/20/2024 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,105.00 – $2,360.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your previous teaching experience. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
