    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35556": {
      "title": "Classroom Organizer (Cabrini or Main Campus)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Classroom Organizer (Cabrini or Main Campus) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Classroom Organizer (Cabrini or Main Campus) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255568V Position Title: Classroom Organizer (Cabrini or Main Campus) Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Driscoll Hall Detailed Work Schedule Classroom Student worker ( CSW ) The Classroom Student Worker is a student position needed daily in the morning from 7:00 AM to 9:00 AM. This position reports to the Classroom Manager/Campus Facilities Inspector. The CSW will be responsible for the classrooms within their assigned building. The CSW will ensure that all furnishings and academic amenities are available in each academic space within their assigned building. Number of positions: 10 Department: 100-Provost Contact Name: Scott Nolan Contact Phone/Extension: 9-5657 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: JOB SUMMARY : Students living on Cabrini’s campus will be CSW for Cabrini classrooms and Students on main will be CSW for main campus. These students will be responsible for the setting and basic maintenance of classrooms throughout the Campus at the onset of each day. Duties assigned are to ensure all furnishings are in proper placement, and clean. Responsibilities are not limited to ensuring that all academic spaces within their assigned buildings but are also well inventoried with necessary amenities- ie- White board markers, eraser, etc… They will see that whiteboards are properly cleaned and erased. They will also ensure that all classroom technology is in proper working order. The CSW will report any issues or concerns regarding technology, cleanliness, and over-operation issues to the Classroom Manager, as well as any needs for custodial assistance. In addition, the CSW will have access to a supply closet that act as a central storage space for all necessary items for the classroom. As this is a new position, it may be necessary to add additional duties to accommodate the needs of this position. JOB DUTIES : 1. Resets academic spaces to be ready for faculty prior to classes. 2. Ensures cleanliness of academic spaces, including but not limited to wiping down and erasing whiteboards, and other furnishings if necessary. 3. Ensures that trash receptacles are empty and that the classroom itself is presentable and neat, i.e. no trash in room, or CSW will request custodial assistance. 4. Restocks classroom amenities as needed, including whiteboard markers, erasers, etc… 5. Reports on issues that require repair within Academic spaces. 6. Will have access to a central location of supplied inventory to replenish classrooms and will advise on replenishing needs to inventory as needed. Requirements: Position is open to all students, This position meets daily from 7AM until 9AM. The student will be expected to report daily and report to classrooms of their assigned building(s). Student will be responsible for ensuring classroom is clean, presentable, furnishings are straightened, and that any amenities, i.e. chalk, markers, erasers are available. When necessary, they will communicate any furniture, custodial, or maintenance issues to the classroom manager. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: The position requires minimal lifting, moving furniture when necessary, considerable walking. The student will be granted access to supply locations to replenish classrooms as needed. Wage Rate: $10.00/hr Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36263": {
      "title": "Student Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Manager - IDEA Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Manager - IDEA Lab To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260376V Position Title: Student Manager - IDEA Lab Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Falvey Memorial Library Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 6 Department: 100-Provost Contact Name: Kirsten Bronkovic Contact Phone/Extension: - Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Work at the Institute for Innovation & Entrepreneurship ( IIE ) where we serve the university to support, encourage, and accelerate innovative thinking and entrepreneurial endeavors. The IIE is looking for team members to support our events, programming, and resources at the IDEA Lab. 3D Printer Manager Maintain the 3D printer, take inventory of supplies and make ordering recommendations. Help fellow students, faculty and staff with the use of the 3D printers. Hold at least two (2) 3D Printer workshops per semester. Must also hold posted office hours for the Villanova community to book equipment time or time for personalized instruction. Maker Space Manager Maintain Glow Forge, take inventory of all supplies in the Maker Space and make ordering recommendations. Help fellow students, faculty and staff with the use of the Glow Forge or any other equipment, supplies or tools in the Maker Space. Make sure that all tools are operational and that there are enough supplies for Maker Space to operate at full capacity and efficiency. Hold at least two (2) Glow Forge workshops per semester. Must also hold posted office hours for the Villanova community to book equipment time or time for personalized instruction. Idea Lab Manager Maintain physical space of the Idea Lab, including but not limited to watering plants, stocking snacks, playing music, cleaning and straightening tables and chairs both inside and outside of the Lab, tracking and ordering supplies, making necessary catering orders for events. Events Manager Responsible for coordinating speaker logistics and for the Innovator’s Supper Club, IIE tabling events across campus, and serve as point person for Idea Challenge and Villanova Student Entrepreneurship Competition ( VSEC ). Plans team building events, including, but not limited to worker bonding day in the fall, graduation BBQ in the spring. In addition to planning, the Events Manager will actively work at these events. Manager of IIE Events & Programs Promote IIE events and programs ensuring brand-alignment and up to date information. Responsible for at least 1 post per week, mirrored across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, LinkedIn, and Wildcat Newswire/Campus Currents, as well as populating Idea Lab screens and website with corresponding content. Manager of Entrepreneur Stories Promote IIE student entrepreneurs, their ventures, and alumni entrepreneurs. Responsible for at least 1 post per week, mirrored across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, LinkedIn, and Wildcat Newswire/Campus Currents. Requirements: Skills in the desired role for which you are applying and an interest in innovation and/or entrepreneurship. Additional Information: TBD Physical Demands Summary: Ability to lift 10lbs Wage Rate: 15/HR Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35995": {
      "title": "Admissions and Outreach Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Admissions and Outreach Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Admissions and Outreach Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260317V Position Title: Admissions and Outreach Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 20 hours/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Vasey Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 576-Dean, Professional Studies Contact Name: Paul Ballentine Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-4366 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The College of Professional Studies is Villanova’s academic home for adult and part-time learners pursuing degree completion, certificates, and continuing education. The Admissions and Outreach Student Worker provides day to day support across the CPS admissions and outreach teams. This role covers a range of responsibilities including: connecting with prospective students and CPS Partner Organizations, preparing materials for recruitment events, strategic communications, event planning, among others. It is a strong fit for a student exploring careers in sales, marketing, communications, or higher education, offering hands on experience with customer relationship management systems, event execution, and direct outreach to prospective students. Requirements: Key Responsibilities Communications Help set up communications tied to events, application deadlines, and other key dates Audit website pages for accuracy and flag outdated content Prospective Student Engagement Assist with answering incoming phone calls Connect with prospective students through inbound and outbound calls to answer questions and direct them to the right resources Inventory and Collateral Oversee admissions and outreach supplies, track quantities, and recommend when reorders are needed Assemble application boxes and organize outgoing mailings Event Support Print name tags, organize and print event materials, and prepare packets for on and off campus events Assist with logistics for on-campus events, including room reservations, food orders, and setup Enter leads from events into Slate Trips, particularly during high volume periods when on the spot entry is not possible Administrative Support Serve as a liaison with the Bursar’s Office as needed for checks, monthly reporting, and vendor forms Complete research assignments such as identifying partner organizations, developing outreach lists, and gathering contact information Qualifications Currently enrolled Villanova student in good standing Interest in sales, marketing, communications, or a career in higher education Comfortable speaking with prospective students by phone in a professional and welcoming manner Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $10 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue 