    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34617": {
      "title": "Student Equipment Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Equipment Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Equipment Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260140V Position Title: Student Equipment Manager Posting Type Student Hours/week: 9-20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Jake Nevin Field House Detailed Work Schedule Students have the opportunity to choose shifts that fit their schedule. Once shifts are chosen, that schedule will be weekly for the remainder of the semester. We ask that each student choose 3 shifts minimum (9 hours weekly), and that all commit to at least one weekend shift (Friday, Saturday or Sunday) Weekday Shifts (M-F): 9am-12pm, 12pm-3pm, 3pm-6pm, 6pm-9pm Weekend Shifts: 9am-12pm, 12pm-3pm, 3pm-6pm, 6pm-9pm Rotating schedule for Friday and Saturday 6pm-9pm shifts Must be able to work at least one weekend shift, weekly Number of positions: 15 Department: 734-Sports - Equipment Contact Name: Nora Toney Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5617 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Assist with the daily operations of the athletic equipment room, including receiving and organizing inventory, managing laundry, distributing gear, and maintaining a clean and organized workspace. Support student-athletes, coaches, and staff with equipment needs and help prepare for practices, competitions, and team travel. Requirements: Ability to work in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Reliable, punctual, and able to commit to scheduled shifts Ability to lift/push/pull and move boxes/equipment (up to ~50 lbs) Willingness to perform physical tasks (laundry, stocking, cleaning) Strong communication skills and positive attitude Ability to follow directions and complete tasks independently Flexibility to work evenings and weekends as needed Respect for equipment policies, confidentiality, and team spaces Additional Information: This is a part-time, on-campus student position for the 2026–27 academic year , students must be enrolled in classes at Villanova to be eligible for this position Work schedules are flexible but may include mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays based on team needs Students must follow all equipment room policies and procedures Training will be provided; no prior experience required Opportunity to work closely with varsity athletic programs and gain hands-on experience in collegiate athletics operations Professional conduct and a team-first attitude are expected at all times Physical Demands Summary: This position requires standing, walking, and moving for extended periods of time. Duties include lifting, carrying, pushing, and pulling equipment and boxes (up to ~50 lbs), as well as frequent bending, reaching, and repetitive motions (laundry, stocking, organizing). The role may involve working in varying temperatures and requires the ability to safely perform physical tasks throughout the duration of assigned shifts. Wage Rate: $10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work anywhere else on campus? If so, how many hours per week? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
