    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35738": {
      "title": "Assistant Costume Shop Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Costume Shop Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Costume Shop Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260365S Position Title: Assistant Costume Shop Manager Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/10-months Avg Hours Week 20 Department: 146-Theatre Position Summary: Under the supervision of Villanova Theatre Department’s ( VTD ) Costume Shop Manager, the Assistant Costume Shop Manager assists with the technical theatre elements related to costumes, hair/makeup, wigs, and all elements of costume design for VTD productions. The primary responsibility of the Assistant Costume Shop Manager is to supervise the day-to-day operations of the costume shop. Responsibilities include leading in the construction and fitting of costumes according to the Costume Design, assisting in the pulling and renting of costume pieces, and assisting in the cleaning, organizing, and storing of all costume pieces. This individual will provide training and guidance to student workers and foster and maintain a safe and healthy work environment. Additionally, the Assistant Costume Shop Manager with serve as costume coordinator for all Villanova Student Theatre ( VST ) and Villanova Student Musical Theatre ( VSMT ) performative events, supervising the pulling of costumes, costume fittings and alterations, load-in, and strike of these productions. The Assistant Costume shop Manager is also responsible for the organization of Villanova Theatre’s costume stock and any rentals of costume pieces. The ideal individual will have a strong drive to provide high-quality work, the ability to exercise good judgment in a variety of situations, strong written and verbal communication, organizational skills, and the ability to work as part of the team which includes student populations. Flexible work schedule required (i.e. occasional evening and weekend work) Duties and Responsibilities: Lead the Costume Build Process for Villanova Theatre Productions: Create patterns for all costumes pieces that will be built in the shop. Utilize student work force as first hands and stitchers. Assist Costume Shop Manager and Costume Designer in scheduling and managing fittings including setting up fitting room and taking/distributing fitting notes. Train and schedule work study and graduate student first hands and stitchers. Communicate with student design assistants regarding scheduling of fittings, fabric and shopping orders, yardages and notions needed per project and professional practices. Lead Technical Coordinator/Costume Shop Supervisor for Student co-curricular groups: Supervise any fittings, alterations, or builds for Villanova Student Theatre ( VST ) and Villanova Student Musical Theatre ( VSMT ) productions. Assist costume shop manager in purchasing, tracking budgets, gathering receipts, and handling returns of all purchased costume elements for these groups. Advise student costume designers on design elements, schedules, and budgets for VST and VSMT productions. Arrange trips to Villanova Theatre’s costume stock with student designers. Attend student group production meetings, design runs, and technical rehearsals as required Organization and Oversight of Villanova Theatre Costume Stock : Assist costume shop manager with organization of costume stock. Serve as primary point person for outside rentals from costume stock Serve as primary point person for costume donations. Attend Villanova Theatre Events when Requested: Events could include show-specific events such as design runs, technical rehearsals, or production meetings. They could also include full department events such as meet and greets, orientations, or other full-staff events. Event attendance will be discussed with the Costume Shop Manager and Production Manager. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned : Duties could include fulfilling rehearsal requests (rehearsal clothing, shoes, etc.), assisting with wig or makeup items, or assisting with the wardrobe team Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Associates Degree. Preferably in theatre design or technology or fashion. Work Experience 2-3 years of experience in costume construction, shop management, or as a shop technician. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Ability to work with individuals of all experience levels. Experience teaching and mentoring students. Strong verbal communication skills. Strong organizational skills and ability to help maintain an inventory of costume shop equipment Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Proficiency in costume construction and alteration techniques Proficiency in draping and pattern making Knowledge of costume crafts, millinery, fabric dying Basic knowledge of purchasing and accounting Equipment Knowledge Operative Knowledge of: All types of home and industrial sewing machines Overlock machines Industrial irons Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education BA or BS in Theatre or fashion with an emphasis in costume construction Work Experience 3-5 years of experience in costume construction, shop management, or working as a shop technician. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Teaching experience a plus Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Costume design experience a plus Wardrobe experience a plus Experience with costume fittings and interacting with actors a plus Equipment Knowledge Experience with 3D Printers a plus Experience with wigs or hair/makeup a plus Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Equipment used: Sewing machines (homemaker and industrial) Overlock machines Steam irons Steamers Fabric scissors Daytime work hours (primary), nights and weekends as assigned. Must be able: to lift and physically move up to 30 lbs. bags of clothing, stand for 5-7 hours a day, withstand finger pricks from pinning clothing to be sewn, sit and sew for 5-7 hours a day if needed. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 07/20/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within hourly grade 12 and the range is $22.36-28.22/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 12 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36078": {
      "title": "Kitchen Supervisor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. Schedule during normal operating hours Friday/Saturday/Sunday/Monday 10am - 9 pm Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260123S Position Title: Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . This leadership position assists the Culinary and Management team in the overall operation of the dining hall/unit. Supervises all personnel, including training and discipline, as well as the preparation and service of food in the unit while adhering to safety and sanitation procedures. Oversees distribution of recipes, work sheets, and production schedules. Assumes opening and closing responsibilities for the unit as required. Assumes responsibility for the kitchen in the chef’s or chef manager’s absence. Ensures food is fresh, well prepared according to the recipes, tasty and well-presented and food production is organized and on track to meet daily demands. This position will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the values of the Villanova Mission and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This position will focus on our Core Values: Sanitation/Safety Friendly Courteous Service, and Excellence. Positions supervised: Associates, Hospitality Associates, General Cooks, etc. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Essential Job Functions: Food Preparation Assists Executive Chef and Chef manager in daily food production. Co -responsibility for the overall food quality. Enforces and supports departmental quality assurance by adhering to VDS best practices for food handling, safety and sanitation. Assures compliance with standard recipes and production methods. Assists in the production and support areas as necessary which includes commissary and catering. Assists chef with the pot sink area including staffing, cleanliness and sanitation procedures. Assistance in the dish room area may also be required. Assists in the training of kitchen staff. Records and monitors food temperatures. Ensures production is organized and on track to meet daily demands, adjusting staff and/or menu as required. Assists leading a kitchen team with support, guidance, positive attitude and good communication skills. Menu Development Recommend changes in procedures and ingredients to assist with menu planning. Test new standardized recipes and make recommendations to the Executive Chef. Continuously research, train, and update techniques, skills and recipes through attending conferences, workshops (including virtual) and reading magazines/journals. Inventory Control Forecast food production quantities of needed products and supplies to ensure proper execution. Complete transfers and requisitions when necessary. Assist in the inventory process to provide accurate reports to assist with food cost analysis. Human Resources and Leadership Provide functional and/or administrative supervision of staff. Provides direction, assignments, feedback, coaching and counseling to assure outcomes are achieved. Assists with Performance reviews. Assists Executive chef and Chef Manager with scheduling. Trains all in safe operating procedures of all equipment and machinery. Includes proper safety training in lifting, carrying, chemical control, first aid and fire prevention/extinguishing. Responsible for opening and/or closing of the unit. Non Essential Job Functions: Performs other duties and assists with projects as assigned including special events for the university and for catering. Assist with scheduling repairs of kitchen equipment, special cleaning projects and pest control management. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Culinary degree/Associate degree or 5 years supervisory kitchen experience. Serv Safe Certification. Work Experience Minimum of 5 years total food service cooking experience preferably in a non fast food environment or high volume operation with progressive responsibilities. Experience with food service software systems. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Excellent written and oral skills. Able to work with a diverse work force. Ability to work independently. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Extensive knowledge of Food Safety and Sanitation. Advanced food preparation and production skills. Ordering and inventory management. Attention to detail in food presentation, flavor and consistency. Proper knife skills ie diced, julienne, chiffonade, mince, etc Equipment Knowledge All kitchen equipment including combi ovens, convection ovens, induction burners, Anliker (Vegetable prep machine), broilers, large batch kettles and slicers, etc. Computer skills required. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in hospitality or culinary field. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used All kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: (any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.) . Exposure to cleaning chemicals, noise, air quality, and ability to withstand temperature extremes in refrigerator and freezer conditions. Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) Ability to lift pots, pans, etc up to 50 lbs. Must be able to stand and exert well-paced mobility for periods for up to 4 hours in length at a time. Special Message to Applicants: The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. Schedule during normal operating hours Friday/Saturday/Sunday/Monday 10am – 9 pm Posting Date: 04/09/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within hourly grade 12 and the range for this position is $21.92-27.36/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 12 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
