    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33401": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Theology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Theology To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Availability of positions is variable and dependent upon numbers of students and courses required. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Candidates selected for interviews for the Adjunct Faculty Pool will be contacted by telephone or e-mail. In accordance with University policy, finalists for this position will be subject to a criminal background check. Unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2015227F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Theology Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 147-Theology/Religious Studies Position Summary: The Department of Theology & Religious Studies seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time to submit a letter of interest (with names and the contact information of three references), a current resume and unofficial copies of college/university transcripts at https://jobs.villanova.edu. Availability of positions is variable and dependent upon numbers of students and courses required. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Candidates selected for interviews for the Adjunct Faculty Pool will be contacted by telephone or e-mail. In accordance with University policy, finalists for this position will be subject to a criminal background check. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Faculty members teach undergraduate or graduate courses in Theology. Minimum Qualifications: Undergraduate courses: Must hold a master’s degree in theology (or related discipline) from an accredited institution of higher education. Previous teaching experience preferred. Graduate Courses: Must hold a doctoral degree in theology (or related discipline) from an accredited institution of higher education. Previous teaching experience preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Availability of positions is variable and dependent upon numbers of students and courses required. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Candidates selected for interviews for the Adjunct Faculty Pool will be contacted by telephone or e-mail. In accordance with University policy, finalists for this position will be subject to a criminal background check. Unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Posting Date: 03/20/2015 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 0 Maximum Number of References Needed 0 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * Do you currently hold a Ph.D. or are you A.B.D? No Response Yes No * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
