    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33437": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Clinical Instructor - Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Clinical Instructor - Nursing To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The College of Nursing will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2014172F Position Title: Adjunct Clinical Instructor - Nursing Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 231-Dean-Nursing Position Summary: Villanova University College of Nursing has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct (part-time) faculty to provide clinical instruction in a variety of clinical courses, including adult medical-surgical nursing; parent child nursing; psychiatric-mental health nursing; and community/public health nursing. Further information about the College of Nursing can be found at www.villanova.edu/nursing. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Understand the course and clinical objectives of the course to which they are assigned and be familiar with the overall curriculum of the College of Nursing. Plan clinical experiences for each student in the clinical group consistent with course and clinical objectives. Provide supervision of students in providing safe, quality patient care. Assist the students to accomplish the clinical objectives of the course. Assist the student to learn clinical decision-making and clinical judgment skills, develop competency in the execution of clinical skills and foster good communication and psychomotor skills with patients, families and other members of the health care team. Validate students’ understanding of theoretical, scientific and evidence based practice to support safe and effective care. Evaluate students’ clinical practice and provide feedback to students on their accomplishment of clinical objectives. Guide students in their growth in the nursing profession. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s in nursing; licensure or eligibility for licensure as a registered nurse in Pennsylvania; experience in clinical specialty area. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in clinical teaching in an academic nursing program; willingness to be flexible in fulfilling responsibilities. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The College of Nursing will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Date: 10/22/2014 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,105.00 – $2,360.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your previous teaching experience. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
