    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35562": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications must be submitted online and should include: Application cover letter, Current and complete curriculum vitae, Statement of teaching philosophy, List of 3 references (we will contact the references for finalists only), Unofficial academic transcripts are required to submit the application. Official transcripts will be required from finalist only. Finalists will be required to submit a statement on their contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments. Mission Statement | Villanova University Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260052F Position Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 241-Law School Instruction Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University Charles Widger School of Law seeks an outstanding lawyer-educator to direct and teach its Intellectual Property (“IP”) Law Clinic. The IP Clinic provides direct representation to entrepreneurs, businesses, and social ventures consistent with the mission of the clinical program, serving client needs in a wide range of intellectual property acquisition, retention, and licensing. Areas of practice may include patent, trademark, copyright and trade secrets, and may include supervision of U.S. P.T.O. certified students engaged in patent and trademark prosecution. Non-patent bar eligible Directors may be asked to work with an adjunct to supervise patent matters. The Director will be a full-time, 12-month continuing non-tenure track (governed by ABA Standard 405©). We anticipate a start date of June 1, 2027. The mission of the Villanova Clinical Program is to teach law students to become competent, reflective, ethical, and creative lawyers committed to seeking justice. Through our teaching and advocacy, we pursue social justice with our clients and surrounding communities by challenging systemic racism, combating inequality, and fostering social change. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach clinic seminar focused on lawyering skills, professional development, and ethical practice, employing clinical teaching methods. Supervise all aspects of student practice while utilizing clinical teaching pedagogy and serve as the attorney of record in Clinic cases when required by the rules of the relevant jurisdiction. Supervision of student practice may include supervision of U.S. P.T.O. certified students engaged in patent and/or trademark prosecution. Oversee all aspects of administration of the IP Clinic, including but not limited to conducting outreach to clients, selecting matters, reporting to funding sources, and maintaining files. Minimum Qualifications: A Juris Doctor degree is required. Pennsylvania bar membership (or an ability to waive into the Pennsylvania bar) is required. Relevant legal practice experience is required. An understanding of, and commitment to, clinical teaching methodology, including an ability to work both collaboratively and independently, is required. A demonstrated interest and/or aptitude for student supervision and teaching is required. Expertise in substantive areas of law relevant to representing and advising clients in a variety of intellectual property acquisition, retention, and licensing needs is required. Excellent oral and written communication skills are required. Preferred Qualifications: Patent Bar membership is preferred. Prior clinical teaching experience or experience supervising law students is preferred. Five years of legal experience is strongly preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All applications must be submitted online and should include: Application cover letter, Current and complete curriculum vitae, Statement of teaching philosophy, List of 3 references (we will contact the references for finalists only), Unofficial academic transcripts are required to submit the application. Official transcripts will be required from finalist only. Finalists will be required to submit a statement on their contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments. Mission Statement | Villanova University Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. Posting Date: 07/06/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Summary of Teaching Evaluations Writing Sample/Publications Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Statement of Contribution to Mission Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36268": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. However, to maximize the chances of success, all required elements of applications should be received by September 15, 2026. All applicants must submit the following required documents: • Cover letter/Letter of application • Curriculum vitae (CV) • Statement of research interests • Statement of teaching philosophy • Copy of graduate transcript • Copies of representative publications • Three confidential letters of recommendation. Recommenders will be contacted via email to submit their letters directly to the application portal. Three letters of recommendation are required. Each recommender will receive an email invitation from the application system, prompting them to submit their letter directly to the system. Important to note that these emails will not be sent until after you have submitted your application, by uploading a cover letter and CV (under the category of “Required Documents”). Your statement of research interests, statement of teaching philosophy, copy of your graduate transcript (unofficial acceptable), and copies of representative publications are also required. However, they are listed below in the category of “Optional Documents”, which gives you the option to upload these documents after submission of the cover letter and CV. Of note, your application will not be reviewed until all required components have been submitted. Again, we recommend that all required elements be submitted by September 15. Other documents in support of your application (e.g., teaching evaluations, syllabi) are optional and must be submitted directly to the portal as “Optional Documents”. If you experience issues with the application portal, please contact the search committee at benjamin.sachs@villanova.edu. An official graduate transcript, a statement on anticipated contributions to the university’s mission and enduring commitments, and other materials will be required from finalists for the position. About the University: Founded in 1842, Villanova University has a total enrollment of about 10,500 students of whom approximately 7000 are full-time undergraduates in one of four colleges: Liberal Arts and Sciences, Engineering, Nursing, and Business. Most of the rest are enrolled in graduate programs in one of the above four colleges or in the School of Law. Location and Accessibility: Villanova University is located approximately 12 miles west of Philadelphia, PA, in the heart of Philadelphia’s suburban \"Main Line\" area. It is readily accessible by car and by public transportation. The campus is located about a quarter of a mile from the Villanova/St. Davids exit of I-476, a major component of the Philadelphia area expressway system. Villanova is connected to Philadelphia and to suburban communities to the west by a SEPTA (Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority) bus line and by the R5 regional rail line which has a station on campus. Another rail line, SEPTA’s Norristown High Speed Line, with two stations on campus, connects Villanova with suburban communities to the north and to the south. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260073F Position Title: Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 143-Psychological and Brain Sciences Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . THE DEPARTMENT OF PSYCHOLOGICAL AND BRAIN SCIENCES at VILLANOVA UNIVERSITY invites applications for TWO TENURE TRACK POSITIONS ( ASSISTANT PROFESSOR ) in NEUROSCIENCE to begin in August 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Neuroscience, Psychology, or a closely related discipline and should have the ability to generate a high-quality research program using non-human model systems and a commitment to teaching in our undergraduate and graduate (M.S.) programs, including mentorship of Master’s theses in our rigorous, research-oriented program. We seek candidates whose research, teaching and service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to excellence of our academic community. For more information about our department and programs, visit http://psychology.villanova.edu. Applications must be submitted at https://jobs.villanova.edu and must include a cover letter, curriculum vita, three letters of recommendation, and other supporting documents as detailed on the application website. An official graduate transcript, a statement on anticipated contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments, and other materials will be required from finalists for the position. Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The search committee may be contacted by email at benjamin.sachs@villanova.edu. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: • Establish and maintain a high-quality research program leading to publication in respected outlets. • Contribute to the department’s teaching efforts, establishing skillful classroom teaching and student mentoring. Teaching responsibilities likely will include Introductory Psychology, Biopsychology, and other assignments determined by faculty member interests and department/program needs. • Provide formal and informal academic advisement to students in accordance with department standards. • Be an active member of our department, college and university. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have earned, or be near completion of, a Ph.D. in Neuroscience, Psychology, or a closely related discipline, with proven achievement or clear aptitude for excellence in research and teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. However, to maximize the chances of success, all required elements of applications should be received by September 15, 2026. All applicants must submit the following required documents: • Cover letter/Letter of application • Curriculum vitae (CV) • Statement of research interests • Statement of teaching philosophy • Copy of graduate transcript • Copies of representative publications • Three confidential letters of recommendation. Recommenders will be contacted via email to submit their letters directly to the application portal. Three letters of recommendation are required. Each recommender will receive an email invitation from the application system, prompting them to submit their letter directly to the system. Important to note that these emails will not be sent until after you have submitted your application, by uploading a cover letter and CV (under the category of “Required Documents”). Your statement of research interests, statement of teaching philosophy, copy of your graduate transcript (unofficial acceptable), and copies of representative publications are also required. However, they are listed below in the category of “Optional Documents”, which gives you the option to upload these documents after submission of the cover letter and CV. Of note, your application will not be reviewed until all required components have been submitted. Again, we recommend that all required elements be submitted by September 15. Other documents in support of your application (e.g., teaching evaluations, syllabi) are optional and must be submitted directly to the portal as “Optional Documents”. If you experience issues with the application portal, please contact the search committee at benjamin.sachs@villanova.edu. An official graduate transcript, a statement on anticipated contributions to the university’s mission and enduring commitments, and other materials will be required from finalists for the position. About the University: Founded in 1842, Villanova University has a total enrollment of about 10,500 students of whom approximately 7000 are full-time undergraduates in one of four colleges: Liberal Arts and Sciences, Engineering, Nursing, and Business. Most of the rest are enrolled in graduate programs in one of the above four colleges or in the School of Law. Location and Accessibility: Villanova University is located approximately 12 miles west of Philadelphia, PA, in the heart of Philadelphia’s suburban “Main Line” area. It is readily accessible by car and by public transportation. The campus is located about a quarter of a mile from the Villanova/St. Davids exit of I-476, a major component of the Philadelphia area expressway system. Villanova is connected to Philadelphia and to suburban communities to the west by a SEPTA (Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority) bus line and by the R5 regional rail line which has a station on campus. Another rail line, SEPTA’s Norristown High Speed Line, with two stations on campus, connects Villanova with suburban communities to the north and to the south. Posting Date: Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Interests Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Writing Sample/Publications Optional Documents Summary of Teaching Evaluations Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
