    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36253": {
      "title": "Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260422S Position Title: Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 604 - University Advancement Position Summary: Ignite Your Career at Villanova University! Whether undergraduate or graduate, faculty or staff, each community member brings with them a wealth of experiences that enrich our University and shift our perspectives. As a part of this community, your work will improve lives and ignite change! Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. · Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. · Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University has embarked on a 10-year strategic plan, Rooted. Restless., with the goal of enhancing the Augustinian Catholic living and learning experience for all members of our community. University Advancement is seeking exceptional talent to join our mission-driven team working together toward our shared vision for Villanova, fueled by the generosity of the University’s philanthropic supporters as we “keep moving” in the spirit of St. Augustine in the public phase of Villanova’s comprehensive capital campaign: Espiritus Nova. Reporting to the Director of Donor Engagement and Recognition, the Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting serves as a key partner in the development and execution of stewardship reporting and donor impact communications across University Advancement. This role collaborates closely with University Advancement Communications ( UAC ), frontline fundraisers, and campus partners to coordinate, develop, and deliver a comprehensive stewardship reporting program that strengthens donor relationships through meaningful, timely, and personalized communications. The Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting , follows workflows, supports content collection and editing, develops reporting templates and tools, and ensures the consistent delivery of donor-centered reports and acknowledgments. This position works directly on the creative content and story creation of high-quality annual donor reports, including but not limited to scholarship reports, custom donor reports, impact statements, endowment reports, fund narratives, and other stewardship communications that demonstrate the impact of philanthropic support. The Stewardship Associate, Communication and Reporting leverages technology and reporting platforms to streamline stewardship processes, improve efficiency, and support customized donor reporting initiatives that align with institutional fundraising and engagement strategies. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Stewardship Reporting and Donor Communications Partner with the Director, UAC , frontline fundraisers, and University stakeholders to coordinate and produce compelling stewardship reports and donor impact communications. Support the editing of endowment narratives, student and donor stories, gratitude statements, and other reporting content necessary for the creation of personalized donor reports. Support development of reporting templates, timelines, and project plans to ensure the timely delivery of endowment reports, scholarship reports, impact statements, fund activation reports, custom stewardship reports, and donor acknowledgments. Serve as a resource to University Advancement staff on stewardship reporting best practices and opportunities for enhanced donor engagement. Digital Stewardship and Reporting Systems Manage digital stewardship outreach through ODDER , FundMiner, AirTable and other reporting platforms in support of donor engagement objectives. Collaborate with University partners and Advancement colleagues to gather content and develop scalable processes for customized donor reporting. Maintain standardized, visually engaging digital report templates and workflows that promote efficiency, consistency, and adherence to stewardship standards. Identify opportunities to enhance donor experiences through digital acknowledgment and reporting strategies. Stewardship Program Development and Collaboration Collaborate with the Director to strengthen and expand stewardship reporting initiatives for principal, major, and leadership-level donors. Partner with University Advancement colleagues to develop tracking and storage mechanisms that support transparent documentation, access and management of stewardship deliverables. Contribute to the development of stewardship policies, reporting standards, metrics, and process improvements that enhance donor engagement and retention efforts. Donor Acknowledgment Communications Collaborate with the Director, UAC and Advancement leadership to develop and maintain acknowledgment templates and communication materials. Draft and coordinate customized stewardship correspondence and acknowledgments on behalf of the Vice President for University Advancement, Advancement leadership, and University leadership as needed. Additional Duties Perform other responsibilities and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. 2-4 years of similar or related experience required. Knowledge of advancement practices, stewardship strategies, and donor communications. Experience creating reports and acknowledgments, synthesizing diverse information, and understanding giving data for individuals, corporations and foundations. Exceptional writing and editing abilities; strong attention to detail; ability to manage multiple projects and shifting priorities; excellent time management; commitment to high‑quality customer service; comfortable working in a fast‑paced environment. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree preferred. Experience with CRMs such as Salesforce and relational databases. Familiarity with Blackbaud Award Management, Banner, Cognos, and FundMiner preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Ability to travel and work some nights/evenings in support of cultivation/recognition events. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 09/02/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 12 and the range is $56,000-62,200. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 12 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33644": {
      "title": "IT Technician I",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | IT Technician I - Learning Technologies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us IT Technician I - Learning Technologies To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255668V Position Title: IT Technician I - Learning Technologies Posting Type Student Hours/week: 20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026 Spring Location Kennedy Hall (Aldwyn 1) Detailed Work Schedule Specific Days and Hours TBD Times between 8AM-5PM (M-F) are preferred. Number of positions: 1-2 Department: 714-UTS - Instructional Technology Contact Name: jessica.diebold@villanova.edu Contact Phone/Extension: (610) 519-3866 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Information Technology Technician I is a student worker role within the University Technology Services ( UTS ) Learning Technologies team. This position supports a technical area and provides an opportunity for students to gain experience in IT operations, documentation, and process improvement. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide Villanova faculty/staff/students with Learning Management System (Blackboard and Brightspace) support and other Villanova supported learning technologies support (e.g. Zoom, Respondus, VoiceThread, etc…) Assist with UTS -Learning Technologies answering and completing service requests from Villanova faculty/students/staff Assist UTS -Learning Technologies staff with projects as needed Contribute to the development and maintenance of documentation and assist in process improvement projects. Other tasks as assigned Requirements: Training for all responsibilities will be provided. Preferred candidates will possess the following skills: • A commitment to excellent customer service • Excellent written and oral communication skills • Comfortable with technology and ability to troubleshoot in Windows, MAC OS, as well as mobile environments • Familiarity with Learning Management Systems (e.g. Blackboard or Brightspace) and video conferencing technology (Zoom) • Ability to work independently with minimal supervision • Dependable once shifts/hours are agreed upon. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 11.25 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
