    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33423": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Management To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Management will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2012078F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Management Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 221-Management Position Summary: The Villanova School of Business ( VSB ) invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Management for undergraduate and MBA courses taught during the day and evening. The department offers programs leading to a BSBA degree. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching specific Management courses. Minimum Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Preferred Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Management or a closely allied discipline is strongly preferred. Master’s degree required. The applicant must be committed to excellence in business education. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Management will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Date: 09/27/2012 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,925.00 – $2,505.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed Maximum Number of References Needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your previous teaching experience. (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34137": {
      "title": "Information Security Intern",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Information Security Intern Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Information Security Intern To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20244997V Position Title: Information Security Intern Posting Type Student Hours/week: TBD (10 hours/week) Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Kennedy Hall Detailed Work Schedule Student must be able to work 2-3 consecutive hours at least 3 days a week (Monday through Friday) on site in the Kennedy Hall building. Working hours between 9 am to 5 pm. Number of positions: 2 Department: 843-UTS - Information Security Contact Name: Ryan Chace and Leonard Nelson Contact Phone/Extension: 610.519.3564 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Information Security Student Intern will work with the Information Security Operations team, with a primary focus on gaining practical experience and knowledge in information security. The Information Security Intern will provide effective user and technical support, particularly in security access controls and guidance for user applications and other systems critical to Villanova University. Under the guidance of members of the Security Operations group, the intern will actively play an integral part in the implementation, remediation, and compliance of technical security across the enterprise. This is a temporary and semester-based position within the Information Security team which offers a valuable opportunity for hands-on learning and skill development in the realm of information security. Technical Support & Maintenance: · Assist members of the Information Security Office with incident and service tickets, including creation and updates of runbooks related to tickets. Support the maintenance of the Application Inventory and related processes to automate and ensure the data in this inventory is accurate. Participate with programming to support procedures and automation of processes within the department. Threat Management and Analysis Aid with threat hunting by leveraging data from key systems and threat intelligence from various sources. Collaborate and support the vulnerability management process including infrastructure and web application vulnerability management scans. Utilize multiple security tools for vulnerability management, unstructured data analysis, and basic security protocols. Documentation, Analysis, and Support: Contribute to the creation and maintenance of documents such as spreadsheets that track, measure, and facilitate improvement of internal processes. Assist with ad hoc projects and initiatives that require analysis and keen desire to learn various tools. Assist with information security awareness activities appropriate for campus audiences Requirements: Minimum: Education A current Villanova University undergraduate student studying Computer Science, Electrical & Computer Engineering, Information Security, Criminal Justice, Information Systems, or related field. Work Experience Completion of coursework relevant to the position, such as courses in information technology, cybersecurity, network security, computer science, or related topics, is required. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Able to maintain confidentiality of security issues Excellent attention to detail Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills Excellent interpersonal skills with a strong commitment to quality Ability to work effectively as part of a highly motivated team Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Microsoft Windows operating systems and processes Functional understanding of application, network, database, physical, and system security and related computer technology and concepts Stays current and maintains effective level of expertise with technology advances in computer security Preferred: Work Experience Knowledge working with support ticket systems Prior internship or work experience in a technical or security-related role. Experience in creating and maintaining documentation to support procedures and processes. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Web and application security skill Vulnerability management and penetration testing skills Operating system proficiency (e.g., Microsoft Windows and Linux) and troubleshooting skills Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Knowledge of programming fundamentals Operating system concepts and system administration knowledge Familiarity with common security tools and technologies, such as vulnerability scanners, SIEM solutions, or network monitoring tools. Other: Demonstrated interest in pursuing a career in information security or cybersecurity. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 15/HR Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35581": {
      "title": "VSB Dean's Office Student Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | VSB Dean&#39;s Office Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us VSB Dean's Office Student Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260256V Position Title: VSB Dean's Office Student Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 6-10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Bartley Hall Detailed Work Schedule Fall 2026 (must be able to work a minimum of 2 closing shifts) Mondays: 8-10:30am, 11:30am-2:30pm, 2-5:00pm Tuesday: 8-10:00am, 3–5:00pm Wednesdays: 8-10:30am, 1:30-3:30pm, 3-5:00pm Thursday 2-4:30pm, 3–5:00pm Fridays: 3-5:00pm Number of positions: 3-4 Department: 216-Dean - Villanova School of Business Contact Name: Denine Super Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5424 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: As a VSB Dean’s Office Student Assistant , you’ll play a vital role in representing Villanova University and fostering a positive campus experience for prospective students, alumni, and guests. You will gain hands-on experience supporting key administrative functions across our Office of Diversity, Equity & Inclusion ( ODEI ), Strategic Initiatives, and Finance & Administration teams. In this role, you will be the first point of contact for visitors, providing excellent customer service. Responsibilities include answering phones, responding to inquiries, managing mail and campus deliveries, maintaining organization of storage supplies, and assisting with a variety of administrative tasks such as data entry, newsletter preparation, and light graphic design. You’ll also support event planning and execution, including setting up materials, coordinating AV equipment, and arranging furniture as needed. What We’re Looking For: We’re seeking a professional, reliable, and detail-oriented student with strong communication and problem-solving skills. The ideal candidate can follow instructions, take initiative, work independently, and maintain a positive and welcoming presence—especially during events. This role may involve light physical tasks such as lifting and moving tables, chairs, and boxes. Requirements: Applicants must be currently enrolled as an undergraduate student at Villanova University; this opportunity is ideal for first- and second-year students. Availability for 6-10 hours per week, with flexibility for special events and occasional Friday shifts, is required. Candidates must be able to commit to working 3 or more of the following shifts each week with 2 or more shifts that end at 5pm. Mondays: 8-10:30am, 11:30am-2:30pm, 2-5:00pm Tuesday: 8-10:00am, 3–5:00pm Wednesdays: 8-10:30am, 1:30-3:30pm, 3-5:00pm Thursday 2-4:30pm, 3–5:00pm Fridays: 3-5:00pm Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Arrange, stack and store furniture on casters for meetings and events. Move storage boxes and organize storage closets. Wage Rate: 10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 08/31/2025 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What semester(s) are you planning to work? Summer/Fall/Spring (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36271": {
      "title": "Barista",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Barista - Local Grounds Cabrini Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Barista - Local Grounds Cabrini To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours Friday/Saturday/Sunday/Monday 3:00pm - 2:00am Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260421S Position Title: Barista - Local Grounds Cabrini Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 412-Dining Services Operations Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Barista is responsible for exceptional customer service at Holy Grounds locations which includes defined level of product knowledge, presentation and quality of product, speed of service, sales ability, and good customer relations skills. Responsible for operating Holy Grounds as an independent unit and assuming all the responsibilities with that role since a manager is not present at all times. This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Provides excellent customer service that is efficient, friendly and speedy to Holy Grounds customers. Treat each customer as your highest priority, being mindful of customers who are waiting. Operates POS terminals and some locations while others use Grub Hub applications to receive orders. Actively shares coffee and tea knowledge while actively selling all products. Advises customers of new coffees or teas or featured items of the week. Prepares all drinks according to Holy Grounds standards. Maintains the cleanliness and attractiveness of the Holy Ground kiosk by keeping counters and displays cleaned and fully stocked. Makes sure all products are labeled correctly. Assist manager with scheduling of student associates. Responsible for enforcing the uniform standards of all student associates. Completes the tasks assigned at each shift, ensuring that everything is ready for the next shift. Enforces and practices all safety and sanitation policies and procedures for Villanova Dining Services. Monitors customer needs and responds to any concerns or questions in a friendly and courteous manner while resolve the issue immediately. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High School diploma or equivalent required. Specific Job Knowledge: Interest in coffee preferred Will need to sample and test products for quality assurance. Minimum Work Experience: Cashiering experience of 1-2 years. Work Skills: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Strong customer service skills. Dress and grooming appropriate for Holy Grounds Concept. Able to handle numerous tasks at once while prioritizing. Equipment Knowledge: Will train on all coffee equipment. Preferred – POS and Grub Hub Systems Preferred Qualifications: Serv Safe certification preferred. Cash register knowledge is preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Espresso machines, grinders, blenders, and cash registers Environmental conditions: Increased noise level around some equipment. Cleaning chemicals used. Physical requirements: Ability to lift up to 30 pounds independently. Ability to sit stand for extended periods. Ability to push/pull up to 30 pounds independently. Ability to use various chemicals. Manual Dexterity. Special Message to Applicants: SCHEDULE during normal operating hours Friday/Saturday/Sunday/Monday 3:00pm – 2:00am Posting Date: Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
