    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31208": {
      "title": "Banquet Bartender",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Banquet Bartender - The Inn at Villanova University Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Banquet Bartender - The Inn at Villanova University To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20210367T Position Title: Banquet Bartender - The Inn at Villanova University Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 507-Inn at Villanova University Position Summary: The Banquet Bartender is responsible for the set-up operation and breakdown of event bars at The Inn at Villanova University. Job duties include preparing and serving alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages. Ability to interact with guests, co-workers, and supervisors in a positive and helpful manner, as well being able to work independently for extended periods of time. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Set up and stock bar area along with preparing any alcoholic or nonalcoholic beverages and condiments/supplies. Greet guests, take customer’s orders and serve in a friendly, courteous manner. Maintain professionalism while assessing guest’s needs and preferences and offer recommendations if needed. Maintain a clean and neat work and service area and restock bar inventory and supplies as needed. Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent required. Basic knowledge of beverages and food items, and cleaning practices, RAMP certification required. 1 year food service experience. Oral and written communication skills. Ability to work independently as well as in a group under general supervision. Excellent guest service skills. Excellent knowledge of in mixing, garnishing and serving drinks. Ability to keep the bar organized, stocked, and clean. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Standing for extended periods of time. Ability to lift a minimum of 30 pounds Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 08/04/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $25.00/hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
