    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36218": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260186V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-20 Eligibility: Work Study ONLY Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 2 Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Contact Name: Moeness Amin Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194363 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Center for advanced Communications, Colllege of Engineering, is offering a 2026/2027 internship for ECE major undergraduates to workin the Radar Lab, Drosdick 006. The work entails learning how to operate mmWave radar, conduct and participate in experiments, processing the data and interpreting the results using signal processing and machine learning. The internship supports around 10-15 hours a week with $15/hour. Please, contact Dr. Moeness Amin moeness.amin@villanova.edu if you are interested. Requirements: Attention to detail; able to follow directions; science major preferred, but not required. Previous lab experience a plus. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 15.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 04/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*)