    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33444": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We will be accepting applications throughout the year and will only fill teaching needs as they arise. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include a letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references), current and complete curriculum vitae, transcripts and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2021835F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Humanitarian Engineering for graduate courses taught in the evening and/or undergraduate courses taught during the day. The Center for Humanitarian Engineering and International Development offers programs leading to a minor in Humanitarian Engineering and offers a series of courses within the graduate program in Sustainable Engineering that includes topics related to international development. It supports research and curriculum development related to sustainable development which is integrated with M.S. degrees and participates in the College of Engineering Ph.D. degree program. The Center for Humanitarian Engineering and International Development was established in 2020 as an outgrowth from the Villanova Engineering Service Learning Program. The Center partners with non-profit organizations globally for the purposes of creating unique experiential learning opportunities for students and faculty wherein outreach efforts are integrated with research and curriculum in support of poverty alleviation and global challenges related to sustainable development. The Center is rooted in ethical engagement with global partners and genuinely believes that partnership, empowerment and humility are key elements of addressing global issues. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary based on the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required. Applicants must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: A doctorate in Engineering or closely allied discipline is strongly preferred. Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: We will be accepting applications throughout the year and will only fill teaching needs as they arise. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include a letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references), current and complete curriculum vitae, transcripts and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: 08/19/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
