    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35420": {
      "title": "Event Technician and Operator",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Event Technician and Operator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Event Technician and Operator To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260241V Position Title: Event Technician and Operator Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Mullen Center Detailed Work Schedule Days/Nights/Weekends Number of positions: 10 Department: 824 - Performing Arts Center Contact Name: Andrea Rumble-Moore Contact Phone/Extension: 96210 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Implement, repair, trouble-shoot, and operate John and Joan Mullen Center for the Performing Arts in technical aspects, including, but not limited to, staging, audio, theatrical lighting, video, safety, and other related production functions for Mullen Center’s performance spaces, classrooms, rehearsal rooms, dance studio, lobbies, and other ancillary rooms. Lighting/Sound/Video Operations (Days/Nights/Weekends) Works with various University departments and student organizations, in particular the Villanova Theatre Department ( VTD ), Academic Departments, Office of Student Life, Office of Music Activities, student groups, alumni organizations, and external clients, coordinating all staff and student efforts to realize the Mullen’s educational and recreational objectives. Reports to the Technical Coordinator/Stage Supervisor I, and Technical Coordinator/Stage Supervisor II to provide periodic updates on progress toward goals, long-range plans, and operational details. Stage Manage or Assistant Stage Manage Mullen Center performances and events, as necessary. Flexibility for last minute work calls and variable work shifts. Requirements: Event experience as it relates to staging, audio, stage lighting, video, rigging, safety, or other related production and event functions. Additional Information: Must be an excellent communicator within an academic environment with an ability to instruct, supervise, and clearly explain technical information, operation, and procedures to diverse audiences (e.g., creative personnel, undergrad and graduate students, production staff, other University departments, academic departments, and external clients.) Excellent customer service skills and proven ability to develop and sustain productive relationships. Physical Demands Summary: Working at heights, lifting up to 50 pounds. Wage Rate: 13/HR Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
