    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34159": {
      "title": "Recreation Marketing Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Recreation Marketing Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Recreation Marketing Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260069V Position Title: Recreation Marketing Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 4-8 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Davis Center Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 2 Department: 775-Athl - Intramurals Contact Name: Ashley Montecchio Vero Contact Phone/Extension: 6105196387 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: · Creating weekly social media posts to cover all areas of the recreation department, including club sports, fitness centers, intramurals, and aquatics. · Managing a social media calendar/schedule via Hootsuite · Maintaining waivers and tracking system for image/likeness usage on recreation marketing materials · Content and design creation for the Villanova recreation website and marketing materials to be dispersed around campus · Creating and publishing a monthly newsletter via MailChimp · Attending biweekly meetings to discuss upcoming marketing needs and projects · Various other marketing projects as assigned Requirements: · Working knowledge of various social media platforms including Facebook, Instagram (including Reels), Twitter, and TikTok – and staying up to date with current social media trends. · Ability to represent the Villanova recreation brand (including university color/verbiage guidelines) in a way that engages the target audience while reflecting Villanova’s mission and values appropriately. · Comfort with various marketing tools/software systems (or willingness to learn how to utilize them) including Canva, Hootsuite, Mailchimp, AEM , etc. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $10/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 04/16/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35629": {
      "title": "Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Office Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260260V Position Title: Student Office Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work Study ONLY Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Garey Hall Detailed Work Schedule Work schedule will be determined between student and Senior Admin. Assistant, depending on student’s academic course schedule. Number of positions: 1 Department: 317-Dept of Global Interdisciplinary Studies Contact Name: Andra Cain Contact Phone/Extension: 6105196302 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Student Office & Social Media Assistant will support the department’s outreach and engagement efforts by managing its social media presence, primarily on Instagram. This role involves attending departmental events to capture content, creating and scheduling daily posts and stories, and assisting with general office tasks. The ideal candidate is creative, organized, and enthusiastic about digital communication and growing the department’s social media presence. Requirements: Social Media Content Creation & Management Develop and post engaging daily content (posts, stories, reels) on Instagram. Maintain a consistent visual and editorial style aligned with the department’s branding. Monitor engagement and respond to comments/messages as appropriate. Event Coverage Attend departmental events (e.g., lectures, student gatherings, workshops) to take photos and short videos. Edit and upload event content in a timely manner. Newsletter Assistance Organize and maintain a list of events, faculty highlights, current student spotlight, and alumni news for the GIS Gazette Planning & Strategy Collaborate with staff, faculty, and Assistant Chair for Critical Languages to plan content around academic calendars, events, and announcements. Maintain a content calendar to ensure regular and strategic posting. Office Support Assist with basic administrative tasks such as room booking, data entry, flyer distribution, office maintenance assistance. Qualifications: Strong familiarity with Instagram and basic photo/video editing tools (e.g., Canva, CapCut, iMovie, etc.). Excellent written communication and visual storytelling skills. Ability to work independently and manage time effectively. Availability to attend occasional evening or weekend events. Preferred Skills: Experience with social media analytics and engagement strategies. Photography or videography experience. Interest in academic or student life communications. Additional Information: We are looking for someone who can take our social media with charge and enthusiasm. Initiative is key in this role as there are many moving parts, and it will require the student to be cognizant, think critically, and act with purpose. Physical Demands Summary: Student will be at desk in the Global Interdisciplinary Studies office and/or at GIS and Program events. Wage Rate: 10.00/hr Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 08/10/2026 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36038": {
      "title": "Official/Scorekeeper",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Official/Scorekeeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Official/Scorekeeper To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please download and complete the New Employee Application by following this link: https://www1.villanova.edu/villanova/recreation/intramurals/employment.html Complete this form and attach it to your application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260288V Position Title: Official/Scorekeeper Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 20 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1-55 Department: 775-Athl - Intramurals Contact Name: Tanner Noble Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-6869 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Do you love sports? Intramurals may be the job for you! Student Employees help facilitate Villanova’s Intramural Sports programs in either an Official/Referee or Scorekeeper role. here….. Requirements: Please complete the IM availability document, and attach to your application as the required “other document” in order to be considered. Additional Information: Please complete the IM availability document, and attach to your application as the required “other document” in order to be considered. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 05/07/2027 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Other Document Optional Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33259": {
      "title": "Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Staff",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Staff Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Staff To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below.  If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20230496T Position Title: Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Staff Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 730-Athl - The Pavilion Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . As a member of the Villanova University staff, Finneran Pavilion Guest Services team members will play a vital role in maximizing the game day experience for Villanova Wildcat fans. Guest Services team members will have the opportunity to work closely with and support the student-athletes, coaching staff, and personnel as they look to continue their tradition of winning. The primary responsibility of the team members is to assist fans in the premium clubs, provide all guests game day specific information, and provide a welcoming environment. All duties must be completed in compliance with University and NCAA rules and regulations. Duties and Responsibilities: Exceed customer service expectations of all Wildcat community members. Understand and practice policies and procedures set by Villanova University Athletics. Attend customer service team member training and maintain comprehensive knowledge of game day information, rules, and regulations. Go above and beyond to enhance game day experience Minimum Qualifications: 18 years of age or older Must be available nights, weekends, and holidays Ability to stand, walk, and climb stairs throughout the duration of the event Required to occasionally lift 10 pounds, unaided. Ability to work well with others Positive attitude toward taking on additional job responsibilities Good judgment Authorization to work in the United States of America Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Ability to stand, walk, and climb stairs throughout the duration of the event Required to occasionally lift 10 pounds, unaided. Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 06/21/2023 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $15.00 per hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tBasketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches?        Y         N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as:\r\n•\tAny person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and\r\n•\tSuch contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU.\r\n\r\nExamples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following:\r\n• Parents/Legal Guardians             \r\n• Coaches (high school, college, club)      \r\n• Personal/Skills Trainers\r\n• Relatives                                          \r\n• Strength Coach                                             \r\n• Advisors\r\n\r\nConsistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any:\r\n•\tCurrent VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes?    Y     N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved.    800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
